1
00:00:05,435 --> 00:00:10,229
[Love in the Moonlight, the show
that illuminated the summer of 2016,]

2
00:00:16,156 --> 00:00:17,541
I shall not allow it.

3
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:20,509
She is mine.

4
00:00:20,509 --> 00:00:25,096
[that left countless iconic lines and scenes]

5
00:00:25,096 --> 00:00:28,382
[had reached a whopping rating of 23.3%]

6
00:00:28,382 --> 00:00:31,456
['Love in the Moonlight' overtakes cable]
[Prince Park Bo Gum takes the world by storm]

7
00:00:31,456 --> 00:00:34,522
['Love in the Moonlight syndrome'
had become a thing of its own.]

8
00:00:34,522 --> 00:00:37,366
[A fan-meeting, carried out as a promise]
If the show reached a rating of over 20%...

9
00:00:37,366 --> 00:00:40,856
[5,000 people in one place!]
the cast promised to hold a fansign in Hanbok.

10
00:00:40,856 --> 00:00:42,880
[Almost a decade ago...]
Thousands of people have come to see it kept.

11
00:00:42,880 --> 00:00:47,553
['Love in the Moonlight' was adored by people]

12
00:00:48,296 --> 00:00:50,842
[And the five youths who made it possible...]

13
00:00:50,842 --> 00:00:53,782
I'm 33 now, so 10 years ago...

14
00:00:53,782 --> 00:00:56,413
[The role that the 23-year-old Bo Gum took on]
I was 23 when I took part in the show.

15
00:00:56,413 --> 00:00:59,759
[Prince Lee Yeong]
It's Lee Yeong. My name.

16
00:00:59,759 --> 00:01:02,225
I'm 27 years old now.

17
00:01:02,225 --> 00:01:04,516
[17-year-old You Jung's role was...]
That means I was 17 at the time.

18
00:01:04,516 --> 00:01:07,219
[Eunuch Sam Nom and crossdresser Ra On]
I, Hong Sam Nom, present to you...

19
00:01:07,219 --> 00:01:08,885
my friendship and devotion.

20
00:01:08,885 --> 00:01:10,412
[25-year-old Jin Young played...]
So, I was 26 years old

21
00:01:10,412 --> 00:01:12,465
[Yoon Seong, the handsome scholar]
or 24, depending on the counting system.

22
00:01:12,465 --> 00:01:14,072
[22-year-old Soo Bin was...]
I think I was 23.

23
00:01:14,072 --> 00:01:17,885
[the snow white maiden, Ha Yeon]
I was counting on meeting you again.

24
00:01:17,885 --> 00:01:20,279
[19-year-old Dong Yeon's part was...]
I was about 20 years old when we filmed it.

25
00:01:20,279 --> 00:01:22,803
[the warrior Byeong Yeon]
You will all fear me.

26
00:01:22,803 --> 00:01:24,465
[Now, after 10 years...]
I can't believe we're...

27
00:01:24,465 --> 00:01:26,496
[Now, after 10 years...]
still working together after a whole decade.

28
00:01:26,496 --> 00:01:31,579
Us five, the five youths
have kept in touch, on good terms.

29
00:01:31,579 --> 00:01:34,405
And I'm proud of that. I really am.

30
00:01:34,405 --> 00:01:37,379
Plans to hang out don't
always work out, you know.

31
00:01:37,379 --> 00:01:40,199
But for us, we always figure out a way
to make time for each other.

32
00:01:40,199 --> 00:01:43,065
[The Moonlight cast has stayed friends...]
We'd work around everyone's schedule.

33
00:01:43,065 --> 00:01:45,399
[for the past 10 years]
We rarely let any one of us miss out.

34
00:01:45,399 --> 00:01:48,212
Well, this 10th anniversary trip...

35
00:01:48,212 --> 00:01:51,796
[Bo Gum took the lead on the trip]
is happening all thanks to Park Bo Gum.

36
00:01:51,796 --> 00:01:53,553
This 10th anniversary trip...

37
00:01:53,553 --> 00:01:55,464
[He had been planning it for a year!]
is a project that I had in mind...

38
00:01:55,464 --> 00:01:57,532
since filming 'Cantabile.'

39
00:01:57,532 --> 00:02:00,885
I liked the idea of the five of us
creating something together.

40
00:02:00,885 --> 00:02:04,563
The number of projects that we had discussed
adds up to around 27,000.

41
00:02:04,563 --> 00:02:07,212
A photoshoot, an OST remake,
and a reality show.

42
00:02:07,212 --> 00:02:10,436
[The anniversary trip was the most loved idea]
I really wanted to make the trip happen.

43
00:02:10,436 --> 00:02:12,852
[A long-time dream,]
I've had it on my mind for a long time.

44
00:02:12,852 --> 00:02:14,312
[the Moonlight cast trip...]
So, with the five of us together,

45
00:02:14,312 --> 00:02:17,361
[starts now!]
I'm very happy to see it happen.

46
00:02:22,665 --> 00:02:26,379
[One fateful hot summer day in August...]

47
00:02:26,379 --> 00:02:29,744
[someone is walking down the road
in the warm sunlight]

48
00:02:29,744 --> 00:02:32,265
[Actor for Lee Yeong, Park Bo Gum]

49
00:02:32,265 --> 00:02:34,165
Hello, everyone.

50
00:02:35,559 --> 00:02:39,039
[At the end of the steep uphill road...]

51
00:02:39,039 --> 00:02:41,552
[Gasp!]
Oh, wow!

52
00:02:44,019 --> 00:02:47,372
[lies a gate, and a surprise beyond it]

53
00:02:48,399 --> 00:02:51,312
[A familiar sight awaits the cast]
No way!

54
00:02:52,792 --> 00:02:56,604
[They are the costumes from 10 years ago!]

55
00:02:56,604 --> 00:02:59,816
[From Prince Lee Yeong's dragon robe]

56
00:02:59,816 --> 00:03:02,652
[to Sam Nom's adorable eunuch robe...]

57
00:03:02,652 --> 00:03:05,643
[and finally, Ra On's beautiful dancing gown]

58
00:03:05,643 --> 00:03:09,389
[the costumes are perfectly preserved
as they were 10 years ago on the set]

59
00:03:10,099 --> 00:03:14,924
[The costume crew treasured these costumes]

60
00:03:18,485 --> 00:03:21,359
Wow, so they really kept these.

61
00:03:23,019 --> 00:03:26,325
[The costumes are bringing back old memories]

62
00:03:26,325 --> 00:03:28,665
They fit right in with the background here.

63
00:03:28,665 --> 00:03:31,739
I can't believe they kept them
in such good condition.

64
00:03:31,739 --> 00:03:34,132
I'm touched.

65
00:03:34,132 --> 00:03:36,032
You seem to be set to a specific mode today.

66
00:03:36,032 --> 00:03:38,479
[The two are in vacation mode]
Yeah, vacation mode.

67
00:03:39,119 --> 00:03:40,632
[They're in a good mood,]
Look, they've got a drone.

68
00:03:40,632 --> 00:03:42,645
[and the right mode]
That's a lot of mosquitoes.

69
00:03:42,645 --> 00:03:44,429
Yeah, some gigantic mosquito, huh?

70
00:03:44,429 --> 00:03:47,785
- I wonder where the set is--oh, what?
- Woah!

71
00:03:47,785 --> 00:03:50,412
- Oh, what?
- Woah!

72
00:03:50,412 --> 00:03:52,232
- Welcome, guys!
- Hello!

73
00:03:52,232 --> 00:03:53,579
- Oh, watch your step.
- Wait...

74
00:03:53,579 --> 00:03:55,119
[Jin Young, as Kim Yoon Seong]
Is there a fee to enter?

75
00:03:55,119 --> 00:03:56,799
[Kim You Jung as Hong Ra On]
How much is it?

76
00:03:56,799 --> 00:03:58,272
- It's free, just for today.
- Oh, my, hello!

77
00:03:58,272 --> 00:03:59,685
[Such bright greetings from
Ra On and Yoon Seong!]

78
00:03:59,685 --> 00:04:01,753
- Oh, wow, it's so pretty!
- Right?

79
00:04:01,753 --> 00:04:03,999
Oh, look what they've got!

80
00:04:03,999 --> 00:04:06,265
Such good memories.

81
00:04:06,265 --> 00:04:09,552
[The red parasol, waiting in the yard]

82
00:04:09,552 --> 00:04:12,332
[10 years ago, under this very parasol,]

83
00:04:12,332 --> 00:04:17,239
[the Yeong & On couple had a secret date!]

84
00:04:20,765 --> 00:04:22,107
Oh, no way!

85
00:04:22,107 --> 00:04:24,912
It's not providing much shade, though.

86
00:04:24,912 --> 00:04:27,945
[The sunlight is strong!]
The sun's not going anywhere.

87
00:04:27,945 --> 00:04:29,290
[Jin Young and You Jung's first encounter...]
So many memories.

88
00:04:29,290 --> 00:04:31,049
[with their costumes from 10 years ago]
These were preserved like this...

89
00:04:31,049 --> 00:04:32,405
- for a decade!
- Wow, that's so cool.

90
00:04:32,405 --> 00:04:35,423
This is how small the robe was?
It felt huge back then.

91
00:04:35,423 --> 00:04:36,711
Yeah, exactly.

92
00:04:36,711 --> 00:04:39,405
[To the 17-year-old Ra On, 10 years ago...]

93
00:04:39,405 --> 00:04:43,532
[the prince seemed so tall and mighty]

94
00:04:43,532 --> 00:04:45,039
I don't remember this gown being this tiny.

95
00:04:45,039 --> 00:04:46,665
[Realizing how small we all were back then]
I don't think I'd fit in it anymore.

96
00:04:46,665 --> 00:04:47,923
I don't think I'd fit in it either.

97
00:04:47,923 --> 00:04:50,659
- We were so little back then.
- We've all bulked up.

98
00:04:50,659 --> 00:04:53,325
They have our pictures over there.

99
00:04:53,325 --> 00:04:56,825
[On the table of the Moonlight crew's
good memories...]

100
00:04:56,825 --> 00:04:59,392
[are photos of the five's younger selves]

101
00:04:59,392 --> 00:05:01,439
What's this?

102
00:05:01,439 --> 00:05:03,276
[A book is on the table as well]

103
00:05:03,276 --> 00:05:07,296
[Lee Yeong's face is on it. What could it be?]
Who drew this?

104
00:05:08,112 --> 00:05:10,372
Oh, it's the book that Ra On wrote!

105
00:05:10,372 --> 00:05:13,539
[It's Ra On's book from the show!]
It's Ra On's book!

106
00:05:13,539 --> 00:05:15,376
[At the end of 'Love in the Moonlight']
In the library, remember?

107
00:05:15,376 --> 00:05:21,725
[Ra On draws Lee Yeong's face
on the novel that she wrote herself]

108
00:05:21,725 --> 00:05:25,019
You said you were writing
the greatest novel ever.

109
00:05:26,865 --> 00:05:28,965
What is this, then?

110
00:05:28,965 --> 00:05:32,672
[The props crew kept it safe
with both of their signatures for 10 years]

111
00:05:32,672 --> 00:05:35,597
They have a secret date at the library, right?

112
00:05:35,597 --> 00:05:38,315
It's actually empty, oops.

113
00:05:40,105 --> 00:05:43,485
It's only visible to those
who are pure of heart.

114
00:05:43,485 --> 00:05:45,345
[The brother and sister...]
Like, on shows like "I am Solo,"

115
00:05:45,345 --> 00:05:48,234
[are having a banter on their way]
it's the male cast that carries the luggage.

116
00:05:48,234 --> 00:05:50,592
- Is that what's happening?
- It's embarrassing to carry this around.

117
00:05:50,592 --> 00:05:53,379
- Oh, look, look!
- Wow, hello, everyone!

118
00:05:53,379 --> 00:05:54,959
[Chae Soo Bin as Jo Ha Yeon]
Hello!

119
00:05:54,959 --> 00:05:56,545
[Kwak Dong Yeon as Kim Byeong Yeon]
Hi!

120
00:05:56,545 --> 00:05:58,545
[The Moonlight cast, reunited at last!]
What are you wearing on your head?

121
00:05:58,545 --> 00:05:59,912
It's too hot!

122
00:05:59,912 --> 00:06:01,549
[Dong Yeon and his mysterious sword]
Where did you get that sword from?

123
00:06:01,549 --> 00:06:02,639
- It's my sword.
- You brought this?

124
00:06:02,639 --> 00:06:04,389
- Yeah.
- What? Is it actually?

125
00:06:04,389 --> 00:06:05,792
[The plastic sword he used for practice]
From the set?

126
00:06:05,792 --> 00:06:06,892
Yeah, the one I used for practice.

127
00:06:06,892 --> 00:06:07,932
- Wow, so cool!
- Oh, I remember.

128
00:06:07,932 --> 00:06:09,412
You still have this?

129
00:06:09,412 --> 00:06:10,857
Well, I actually didn't mean to,

130
00:06:10,857 --> 00:06:12,392
[He stole it from the action school]
but I kind of stole it.

131
00:06:12,392 --> 00:06:13,705
Right, he forgot to return it.

132
00:06:13,705 --> 00:06:14,963
- Oh, he forgot.
- Forgot to give it back?

133
00:06:14,963 --> 00:06:16,340
[The sun is blazing at 37 degrees]
Wow, wait a minute.

134
00:06:16,340 --> 00:06:18,161
It's scorching hot out.

135
00:06:19,813 --> 00:06:22,431
[Byeong Yeon the warrior springs to action]
Not bad, honestly.

136
00:06:22,431 --> 00:06:23,480
[Soo Bin and Dong Yeon...]
Come look at this.

137
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:25,047
[joins the yard tour]
This is awesome!

138
00:06:25,047 --> 00:06:27,553
- So cool.
- Go put on the bracelets over there.

139
00:06:27,553 --> 00:06:28,957
- See those bracelets?
- What are these?

140
00:06:28,957 --> 00:06:30,008
[Lee Yeong and Ra On's ship name...]
Yeong On bracelets.

141
00:06:30,008 --> 00:06:32,633
[Yeong On themed bracelets]
They prepared five of them.

142
00:06:32,633 --> 00:06:33,873
[The Yeong On bracelet,]
From now on, you are...

143
00:06:33,873 --> 00:06:36,980
[a symbol of the two lovers' devotion]
the most cherished lady in the entire world.

144
00:06:37,780 --> 00:06:39,180
[Now a symbol of the five friends]
Let's make a moon shape.

145
00:06:39,180 --> 00:06:40,697
- Oh, like this? Okay.
- What's that?

146
00:06:40,697 --> 00:06:43,033
- What is that?
- Sorry.

147
00:06:43,033 --> 00:06:44,853
One, two, three.

148
00:06:44,853 --> 00:06:47,007
[They made a full moon with their hands]
Two, three...

149
00:06:47,880 --> 00:06:49,532
Wow, it's been such a long time.

150
00:06:49,532 --> 00:06:50,927
I'm flooded with memories.

151
00:06:50,927 --> 00:06:55,134
Do each of you remember
any stories or scenes from these costumes?

152
00:06:55,134 --> 00:06:57,941
This gown was a dancing gown.

153
00:06:58,627 --> 00:07:02,060
[Ra On's solo dance]

154
00:07:02,060 --> 00:07:03,347
[Lee Yeong's cosmos field finale]
This is from the finale.

155
00:07:03,347 --> 00:07:05,937
Yeah, the robe from the finale.
In the cosmos field.

156
00:07:05,937 --> 00:07:07,897
[Ra On in Yoon Seong's arms]
This one's from when Ra On...

157
00:07:07,897 --> 00:07:09,907
tried to catch a chicken and fell.

158
00:07:09,907 --> 00:07:12,033
[Ha Yeon and Lee Yeong's first encounter]
I think that one's from my first appearance.

159
00:07:12,033 --> 00:07:14,520
I remember wearing it on my first day.

160
00:07:14,520 --> 00:07:15,773
[Byeong Yeon's warrior robe]
Oh, look how worn this is.

161
00:07:15,773 --> 00:07:17,393
It's fake leather, and yet...

162
00:07:18,156 --> 00:07:20,553
Wait, this brand was the rage back then, too?

163
00:07:20,553 --> 00:07:21,880
[Turns out Byeong Yeon
liked to wear Italian leather]

164
00:07:21,880 --> 00:07:23,263
That's hilarious!

165
00:07:23,263 --> 00:07:24,820
- I guess Byeong Yeon was the blueprint.
- May I?

166
00:07:24,820 --> 00:07:26,249
Look at this.

167
00:07:26,249 --> 00:07:29,980
[Warrior Byeong Yeon steals
Yoon Seong the rich kid's expensive bag]

168
00:07:29,980 --> 00:07:32,620
[The man with both a sword and a luxury bag]

169
00:07:32,620 --> 00:07:34,237
He was a true fashionista.

170
00:07:34,237 --> 00:07:35,708
[Joseon trendsetter look]
A Joseon fashionista.

171
00:07:35,708 --> 00:07:37,624
Joseon fashion guru!

172
00:07:38,247 --> 00:07:41,144
[By the end of the trip...]

173
00:07:41,144 --> 00:07:42,833
[the Moonlight cast is back in their costumes]
My name is Hong Ra On, your highness.

174
00:07:42,833 --> 00:07:45,853
You are my whole world, Ra On.

175
00:07:45,853 --> 00:07:47,217
[It's as if they went back in time]
It feels so weird.

176
00:07:47,217 --> 00:07:48,527
- Feels like we've gone back to the past.
- Yeah.

177
00:07:48,527 --> 00:07:51,190
It's like wearing your old school uniform.

178
00:07:51,190 --> 00:07:52,734
- It's a strange feeling.
- Yeah, it's odd.

179
00:07:52,734 --> 00:07:54,197
It feels so weird.

180
00:07:55,313 --> 00:07:57,113
How about we head inside? It'll be cooler.

181
00:07:57,113 --> 00:07:59,367
- Oh, yeah!
- Let's see what it's like inside.

182
00:07:59,367 --> 00:08:00,780
Wait, let's take a photo here.

183
00:08:00,780 --> 00:08:02,240
Ah, yep, yep.

184
00:08:02,240 --> 00:08:05,066
- With these little guys.
- Sure, sure.

185
00:08:05,066 --> 00:08:09,834
[Photo time with their long-lost costumes]
So cute.

186
00:08:11,760 --> 00:08:12,760
[Wink]

187
00:08:13,593 --> 00:08:15,907
[Photo break is over]
- Thank you! - Thank you!

188
00:08:15,907 --> 00:08:17,767
Thanks.

189
00:08:17,767 --> 00:08:18,987
Let's take a selfie, too.

190
00:08:18,987 --> 00:08:20,253
- Oh, okay.
- All together.

191
00:08:20,253 --> 00:08:21,531
Let's take a selfie, too.

192
00:08:21,531 --> 00:08:22,787
- Oh, okay.
- All together.

193
00:08:22,787 --> 00:08:24,764
[Gathering for selfies like second nature]

194
00:08:24,764 --> 00:08:25,988
[Fun fact: Bo Gum loves taking pictures,]
Serial photo-takers, for real.

195
00:08:25,988 --> 00:08:28,423
[and is the photographer of the group.]
One, two, three.

196
00:08:29,973 --> 00:08:33,593
[The Moonlight cast welcomes
all of Bo Gum's photographic whims]

197
00:08:34,567 --> 00:08:36,293
[At last, everyone is entering the lodging]

198
00:08:36,293 --> 00:08:37,996
- Oh, it's cool in here!
- So pretty!

199
00:08:38,680 --> 00:08:41,940
[Located in the middle of a mountain...]

200
00:08:41,940 --> 00:08:46,347
[is our amazing Hanok resort]

201
00:08:47,600 --> 00:08:49,997
[A welcoming living room
for the Moonlight cast...]

202
00:08:49,997 --> 00:08:51,867
[Love in the Moonlight]

203
00:08:51,867 --> 00:08:53,987
Wow, what's all this?

204
00:08:53,987 --> 00:08:55,980
[A welcome pot of lotus tea]
I think it's lotus tea!

205
00:08:55,980 --> 00:08:58,253
[and yakgwa of fond memories]
It's so pretty!

206
00:08:59,167 --> 00:09:00,971
- Let's have a toast.
- Alright.

207
00:09:00,971 --> 00:09:03,262
- I'm so glad we're all together again.
- It feels like we're drinking.

208
00:09:03,262 --> 00:09:06,533
- Here's to a nice vacation!
- A nice vacation.

209
00:09:07,493 --> 00:09:09,542
[A cup of fragrant lotus tea
in wishes for an enjoyable vacation]

210
00:09:09,542 --> 00:09:11,979
- It's quite savory.
- It tastes good.

211
00:09:11,979 --> 00:09:14,387
- What's this? Are we allowed to open it?
- I think it's a present.

212
00:09:14,387 --> 00:09:15,871
[A welcome gift on the table]
Love in the Moonlight: Redrawn?

213
00:09:15,871 --> 00:09:17,101
Open!

214
00:09:17,101 --> 00:09:18,627
That's a big watch.

215
00:09:18,627 --> 00:09:20,124
Oh, what's this?

216
00:09:20,124 --> 00:09:21,520
[A film camera, a camcorder, and portable fans]
Oh, look, fans!

217
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:23,327
- Wow, a camera!
- It's a camera.

218
00:09:23,327 --> 00:09:25,013
We can take pictures with this now.

219
00:09:25,013 --> 00:09:27,197
- I'll take the camcorder, then.
- The camcorder?

220
00:09:27,197 --> 00:09:29,708
[What memories will this camera hold?]
I'll take the camera, then.

221
00:09:29,708 --> 00:09:35,067
[Preview of the camcorder]
Is it working?

222
00:09:35,067 --> 00:09:37,180
[The Moonlight cast's
adorable activities will be recorded]

223
00:09:37,180 --> 00:09:38,813
You have to do a little dance, like so.

224
00:09:38,813 --> 00:09:40,577
Tomato pasta.

225
00:09:40,577 --> 00:09:43,302
If you don't play, you lose,
rock, paper, scissors!

226
00:09:43,302 --> 00:09:44,467
[The portable fans are one for each]
I'll just take a fan.

227
00:09:44,467 --> 00:09:46,717
- I like them.
- The fan...

228
00:09:46,717 --> 00:09:48,767
[They turn the fans on to find...]
Let me see.

229
00:09:48,767 --> 00:09:52,387
[that the wings reveal texts!]
Look, right there!

230
00:09:52,387 --> 00:09:56,060
- Look, right there!
- Wow, wow, wow!

231
00:09:56,060 --> 00:09:58,804
- A ferocious herbivore...
- Wow, technology sure has advanced.

232
00:09:58,804 --> 00:10:03,635
[The words on the fans are...]
Wow, technology sure has advanced.

233
00:10:03,635 --> 00:10:06,880
[Ferocious Herbivore]
Like a ferocious herbivore.

234
00:10:06,880 --> 00:10:09,600
[School President]
Vibes of a school president.

235
00:10:09,600 --> 00:10:11,891
[Youngest Uncle]
I'd say... like a youngest uncle?

236
00:10:11,891 --> 00:10:13,073
[Dr. Oh Eun Young]
Like Dr. Oh Eun Young.

237
00:10:13,073 --> 00:10:14,253
[The nicknames they gave each other
during the pre-interview]

238
00:10:14,253 --> 00:10:16,673
[Perfect Tease]
Just perfect to tease.

239
00:10:16,673 --> 00:10:18,500
[Only the name giver knows who owns each fan]
Youngest uncle?

240
00:10:18,500 --> 00:10:21,033
- Youngest uncle...
- Dr. Oh Eun Young, too?

241
00:10:21,033 --> 00:10:23,347
[Youngest uncle, Dr. Oh, school president,
perfect tease, ferocious herbivore]

242
00:10:23,347 --> 00:10:26,127
A school president, a perfect tease...

243
00:10:26,127 --> 00:10:28,524
A perfect tease... and a ferocious herbivore?

244
00:10:28,524 --> 00:10:30,687
[Time to find the owner of each fan]
A ferocious herbivore.

245
00:10:30,687 --> 00:10:31,967
[Ferocious herbivore]
This one's obvious.

246
00:10:31,967 --> 00:10:33,357
Who is it?

247
00:10:33,357 --> 00:10:34,977
- Isn't it Soo Bin?
- Me?

248
00:10:35,960 --> 00:10:38,220
- Am I ferocious?
- Well, no, but...

249
00:10:38,220 --> 00:10:40,697
She's obviously a herbivore...

250
00:10:40,697 --> 00:10:42,680
but who called her ferocious?

251
00:10:42,680 --> 00:10:45,460
Like a ferocious herbivore.

252
00:10:45,460 --> 00:10:48,247
She's very good to tease
because she has a big reaction.

253
00:10:48,247 --> 00:10:50,173
[Loud but harmless]
But if you listen to what she's saying...

254
00:10:50,173 --> 00:10:51,860
she just isn't very good at threatening.

255
00:10:51,860 --> 00:10:54,237
So why am I a ferocious herbivore?

256
00:10:54,237 --> 00:10:56,041
- You're doing it right now.
- Look at yourself.

257
00:10:56,041 --> 00:10:58,753
- The way she's asking, right?
- Yeah, like, "why am I a ferocious..."

258
00:10:58,753 --> 00:10:59,967
[A sneak peek at the ferocious herbivore]
Eat it with rice...

259
00:10:59,967 --> 00:11:01,727
[Being loud]
Quiet down!

260
00:11:01,727 --> 00:11:05,536
[Just one more chance, please!]
Give me another chance!

261
00:11:06,320 --> 00:11:07,784
[Talking about a restaurant visit
after a photoshoot for a poster]

262
00:11:07,784 --> 00:11:09,761
Yeah, I think it was
after that poster photoshoot.

263
00:11:09,761 --> 00:11:12,687
Wait, I was at that photoshoot, too.
Why didn't I get invited?

264
00:11:12,687 --> 00:11:14,891
[Turns out it was a different day]
I guess it was a different day.

265
00:11:14,891 --> 00:11:17,107
[Isn't afraid to talk, but isn't scary either]
That was such a fast remark.

266
00:11:17,107 --> 00:11:18,127
No, seriously.

267
00:11:18,127 --> 00:11:20,187
Who's Dr. Oh Eun Young, then?

268
00:11:20,187 --> 00:11:22,097
Wait, isn't that You Jung?

269
00:11:22,097 --> 00:11:23,477
[Is You Jung's nickname 'Dr. Oh Eun Young'?]
It feels right, yeah.

270
00:11:23,477 --> 00:11:24,507
Is that who I am?

271
00:11:24,507 --> 00:11:26,211
[Or is it 'School President'?]
Maybe You Jung is the school president.

272
00:11:26,211 --> 00:11:27,240
[No one is agreeing]
I don't think so.

273
00:11:27,240 --> 00:11:28,487
[So who is which?]
What if I'm Dr. Oh Eun Young?

274
00:11:28,487 --> 00:11:30,287
- Take this, then.
- Are you Dr. Oh?

275
00:11:30,287 --> 00:11:32,740
- Take this, then.
- Are you Dr. Oh?

276
00:11:32,740 --> 00:11:34,104
[You Jung: Dr. Oh Eun Young]
I'm Dr. Oh Eun Young?

277
00:11:34,104 --> 00:11:35,128
Who gave me this nickname?

278
00:11:35,128 --> 00:11:37,019
[Jin Young did it]
It was me.

279
00:11:37,019 --> 00:11:38,900
- You're the school president.
- Oh, really?

280
00:11:38,900 --> 00:11:40,760
[Bo Gum: School President]
It's you.

281
00:11:40,760 --> 00:11:43,320
But I want to be Dr. Oh Eun Young.

282
00:11:44,833 --> 00:11:46,153
Dr. Oh Eun Young.

283
00:11:46,153 --> 00:11:48,493
She can scold even those older than her.

284
00:11:48,493 --> 00:11:50,513
There's just this aura about her.

285
00:11:50,513 --> 00:11:51,537
[Rascal #1, ordering a diet coke]
Do you have diet coke?

286
00:11:51,537 --> 00:11:52,760
It'll trick your body...

287
00:11:52,760 --> 00:11:55,331
[Dr. Oh, considerate of the rascals' health]
into thinking it didn't get any sugar.

288
00:11:55,331 --> 00:11:59,180
[Did research on what they need for dinner]
I looked up all the ingredients for baeksuk.

289
00:11:59,180 --> 00:12:00,747
[Rascal #2, who has a different menu in mind]
I want potato fritters. Can we just have that?

290
00:12:00,747 --> 00:12:02,340
That, or kimchi pancake.

291
00:12:02,340 --> 00:12:03,597
Alright, we can do potato fritters.

292
00:12:03,597 --> 00:12:06,787
[Dr. Oh presents an easy-breezy solution]
And if we have time, kimchi pancake as well.

293
00:12:06,787 --> 00:12:09,120
[Soo Bin named Bo Gum]
Bo Gum is... like a school president.

294
00:12:09,120 --> 00:12:11,147
I'm probably the school president.

295
00:12:11,147 --> 00:12:14,907
[Everyone admits he's the school president]
I'm just inclined to guide our group.

296
00:12:14,907 --> 00:12:16,593
This whole thing was your idea, anyway.

297
00:12:16,593 --> 00:12:18,457
[President Park's feat #1: planning the trip]
Exactly.

298
00:12:18,457 --> 00:12:20,427
[President Park's feat #2: a spoon of romance]
This feels like a photoshoot in itself.

299
00:12:20,427 --> 00:12:22,087
I hope our friendship lasts forever.

300
00:12:22,087 --> 00:12:23,880
- May I buy this?
- Nope.

301
00:12:23,880 --> 00:12:25,200
[President Park's feat #3: no wasting money]
But why? Just one, please?

302
00:12:25,200 --> 00:12:26,871
- No, don't buy it.
- But why?

303
00:12:26,871 --> 00:12:28,953
- I want some thrill.
- Oh, you want a thrill?

304
00:12:28,953 --> 00:12:30,827
Nuh-uh.

305
00:12:30,827 --> 00:12:32,793
[Can't sit by and watch the cast be reckless]
Too dangerous.

306
00:12:32,793 --> 00:12:34,540
[Is Jin Young the youngest uncle?]
Just take this.

307
00:12:34,540 --> 00:12:35,474
It's not him!

308
00:12:35,474 --> 00:12:36,953
[Take it]
The youngest uncle...

309
00:12:36,953 --> 00:12:38,533
[You Jung named Dong Yeon 'Youngest Uncle']
The youngest uncle...

310
00:12:38,533 --> 00:12:40,097
What, me?

311
00:12:40,097 --> 00:12:41,320
I came up with it.

312
00:12:41,320 --> 00:12:42,827
Oh, really? So he's the great uncle, or what?

313
00:12:42,827 --> 00:12:45,413
Dong Yeon is a jokester.

314
00:12:45,413 --> 00:12:47,420
- Boo!
- Boo.

315
00:12:47,420 --> 00:12:48,607
The three seniors.

316
00:12:48,607 --> 00:12:50,557
[Senior #1, #2, #3]
The three seniors?

317
00:12:50,557 --> 00:12:52,033
[Likes to make fun of people
like the youngest uncle of the family]

318
00:12:52,033 --> 00:12:53,993
Toodles, stragglers!

319
00:12:53,993 --> 00:12:55,573
One of us will have to give up a drumstick.

320
00:12:55,573 --> 00:12:56,857
I can give it up.

321
00:12:56,857 --> 00:12:57,881
- Me, too.
- I don't have to eat one.

322
00:12:57,881 --> 00:12:59,766
Alright, then, can I have three?

323
00:12:59,766 --> 00:13:01,130
Sexy dynamite!

324
00:13:01,130 --> 00:13:03,433
[The shame is for his friends to bear]

325
00:13:03,433 --> 00:13:05,073
[Lastly, Jin Young is the perfect tease]
Over there, 'perfect tease'.

326
00:13:05,073 --> 00:13:06,233
- That's me?
- Yeah.

327
00:13:06,233 --> 00:13:07,864
- But why?
- Well, you are good to poke fun at.

328
00:13:07,864 --> 00:13:10,873
- You're really fun to tease.
- Am I?

329
00:13:10,873 --> 00:13:12,251
These guys...

330
00:13:12,251 --> 00:13:13,953
They love to make fun of me.

331
00:13:13,953 --> 00:13:15,340
And the center of all evil...

332
00:13:15,340 --> 00:13:16,951
is Dong Yeon and You Jung.

333
00:13:16,951 --> 00:13:19,560
[Doesn't even deny it]
I do tease him a lot.

334
00:13:19,560 --> 00:13:22,800
He really makes me put myself on trial.

335
00:13:22,800 --> 00:13:25,320
I keep wondering how much he'd put up with me.

336
00:13:25,320 --> 00:13:26,686
[Source of all evil #1 and #2]
Well? What am I?

337
00:13:26,686 --> 00:13:27,707
[Unfortunately the 'Perfect Tease'
is seated between these two]

338
00:13:27,707 --> 00:13:29,391
There's no explanation needed, is there?

339
00:13:29,391 --> 00:13:31,840
Clearly something went wrong
somewhere along the way.

340
00:13:31,840 --> 00:13:34,304
- I think I know where it went wrong.
- Well? Tell me.

341
00:13:34,304 --> 00:13:37,521
- I think it started with ghosts.
- Oh, true.

342
00:13:37,521 --> 00:13:39,740
I'm scared of ghosts.

343
00:13:39,740 --> 00:13:42,177
One time, they came over to my place.

344
00:13:42,177 --> 00:13:45,148
It was a duplex with a basement.

345
00:13:45,148 --> 00:13:48,320
He started to say that he kept hearing sounds.

346
00:13:48,320 --> 00:13:49,907
So we all joined in on it.

347
00:13:49,907 --> 00:13:52,480
Like, "I think I actually hear something."

348
00:13:52,480 --> 00:13:53,884
He was terrified.

349
00:13:53,884 --> 00:13:57,273
Then, Jin Young asked me to stay over.

350
00:13:57,273 --> 00:13:59,377
- Just how scared were you?
- But...

351
00:13:59,377 --> 00:14:00,831
Isn't everyone afraid of ghosts?

352
00:14:02,707 --> 00:14:03,993
[I dare any ghost lovers to come forth!]
Seriously, does anyone like ghosts?

353
00:14:03,993 --> 00:14:05,033
Who likes ghosts anyway?

354
00:14:05,033 --> 00:14:06,540
Well, nobody likes them, of course.

355
00:14:08,113 --> 00:14:09,293
[Seriously contemplating]
But...

356
00:14:09,293 --> 00:14:10,687
I guess it is scary, if you think about it.

357
00:14:10,687 --> 00:14:12,231
Imagine you're all alone.

358
00:14:12,231 --> 00:14:13,607
[Snicker]
And that place...

359
00:14:13,607 --> 00:14:15,127
[The president is trying hard to comfort him]
did have a spooky vibe to it.

360
00:14:15,127 --> 00:14:17,193
- He's being an empath!
- But that place was kind of spooky, yeah.

361
00:14:17,193 --> 00:14:18,793
- Yeah, that's true.
- It was.

362
00:14:18,793 --> 00:14:20,360
You gave a proper goodbye
when you moved out, right?

363
00:14:20,360 --> 00:14:21,527
No, they moved together.

364
00:14:21,527 --> 00:14:22,551
Don't say that.

365
00:14:22,551 --> 00:14:23,987
[The two pinnacles of evil, making their move]
Oh, it's the same ghost, then?

366
00:14:23,987 --> 00:14:25,412
- Like, in his house, now?
- Yeah, the same one.

367
00:14:25,412 --> 00:14:28,280
You'll be fine.
You're sleeping with us tonight.

368
00:14:28,280 --> 00:14:31,180
So now we change and go eat, right?

369
00:14:31,180 --> 00:14:33,804
[They're changing to go rafting]
Yeah, let's change.

370
00:14:33,804 --> 00:14:35,407
But, like, rafting and stuff...

371
00:14:35,407 --> 00:14:37,313
won't get you wet or anything, right?

372
00:14:37,313 --> 00:14:38,600
- Of course you'll get wet.
- Yeah, you will.

373
00:14:38,600 --> 00:14:40,473
- Why?
- It's a water sport, duh.

374
00:14:40,473 --> 00:14:42,464
We'll be in the water.

375
00:14:42,464 --> 00:14:46,055
- You might fall off the raft, too.
- The river here in Hongcheon is rough.

376
00:14:46,055 --> 00:14:48,587
- That won't do.
- What's wrong? Didn't pack your swimming suit?

377
00:14:48,587 --> 00:14:49,884
No, it's not that.

378
00:14:49,884 --> 00:14:51,773
- What is it, then?
- Well, the water...

379
00:14:51,773 --> 00:14:52,997
- Are you scared?
- Of falling in!

380
00:14:52,997 --> 00:14:54,227
- You're scared of water?
- Of falling in.

381
00:14:54,227 --> 00:14:55,564
[There's no way he's not getting teased]

382
00:14:55,564 --> 00:14:57,760
[Dying of laughter]
Well, Bo Gum is...

383
00:14:57,760 --> 00:14:59,131
- He's a great swimmer.
- Yeah?

384
00:14:59,131 --> 00:15:00,780
- He'll save you for sure.
- Oh, okay. Okay.

385
00:15:00,780 --> 00:15:02,647
- Don't worry too much about it.
- I believe you.

386
00:15:02,647 --> 00:15:04,600
[He is indeed a perfect tease]
This is gold.

387
00:15:04,600 --> 00:15:06,527
- Don't worry about it.
- There are four of us here.

388
00:15:06,527 --> 00:15:08,378
[Oh Eun Young(27) / Ph.D.]
What are you worried about?

389
00:15:08,378 --> 00:15:11,201
We have life vests, too.

390
00:15:12,540 --> 00:15:13,693
[The Moonlight cast are ready to go]
Shall we go now?

391
00:15:13,693 --> 00:15:15,167
Shall we?

392
00:15:15,167 --> 00:15:18,080
Why not take another photo before we go?

393
00:15:18,080 --> 00:15:19,371
[Moonlight photographer, on the move]
It's going to turn out backlit.

394
00:15:19,371 --> 00:15:21,338
[Moonlight photographer, on the move]
How about now?

395
00:15:22,660 --> 00:15:27,487
[Snap snap with a beating heart
before the vacation officially starts]

396
00:15:28,267 --> 00:15:29,793
[Bo Gum's choice of restaurant for lunch]
Is this the place you told me about?

397
00:15:29,793 --> 00:15:30,793
Yes.

398
00:15:32,587 --> 00:15:34,080
They've got all sorts of stuff on the menu!

399
00:15:34,080 --> 00:15:36,360
- Boneless short rib sounds good.
- Boneless short rib!

400
00:15:36,360 --> 00:15:38,307
Octopus on a griddle must be good, too.

401
00:15:38,307 --> 00:15:40,540
Oh, and cold noodles as a palate cleanser.

402
00:15:40,540 --> 00:15:41,953
[And potato pancakes, You Jung's choice]
Oh, potato pancakes!

403
00:15:41,953 --> 00:15:43,691
- One potato pancake, please.
- Alright.

404
00:15:43,691 --> 00:15:45,047
Did you answer this in the pre-interview, too?

405
00:15:45,047 --> 00:15:46,893
So who do you think would get married first?

406
00:15:46,893 --> 00:15:47,833
- What? No!
- They didn't ask me that.

407
00:15:47,833 --> 00:15:49,453
[All four except Bo Gum have no idea]
They asked that?

408
00:15:49,453 --> 00:15:50,544
- They didn't ask you?
- No.

409
00:15:50,544 --> 00:15:51,927
So? What did you say?

410
00:15:51,927 --> 00:15:53,840
- First place was You Jung.
- Me?

411
00:15:53,840 --> 00:15:55,260
First place was You Jung.

412
00:15:55,260 --> 00:15:56,533
[You Jung, the youngest, the fastest to marry?]
Me?

413
00:15:56,533 --> 00:15:58,743
- Wait, why me?
- Yeah, why her?

414
00:15:58,743 --> 00:16:00,353
[The others are surprised to hear this, too]
Why me?

415
00:16:00,353 --> 00:16:01,713
Why, why me?

416
00:16:01,713 --> 00:16:03,557
I'm the youngest here!

417
00:16:03,557 --> 00:16:05,581
- Why?
- Well, I think you're the most likely...

418
00:16:05,581 --> 00:16:08,713
[The clever youngest]
to meet a good person and get married.

419
00:16:08,713 --> 00:16:10,960
Then who do you think would be the last?

420
00:16:10,960 --> 00:16:13,077
The last, huh?

421
00:16:15,013 --> 00:16:17,113
[Gaze goes towards the oldest of them all]
Wait, no, not him!

422
00:16:17,113 --> 00:16:18,977
[Why is he looking at me?]

423
00:16:18,977 --> 00:16:20,854
[Finishes him off with another glance]

424
00:16:20,854 --> 00:16:22,409
[Perfect tease]
Why? What, why me?

425
00:16:22,409 --> 00:16:24,790
[Just making fun of the eldest]
Oh, I'm just kidding.

426
00:16:24,790 --> 00:16:27,334
I don't think anyone's going to marry too late.

427
00:16:27,334 --> 00:16:29,486
It'd feel so weird, though.

428
00:16:29,486 --> 00:16:31,993
- If any of us got married, you know.
- Yeah.

429
00:16:31,993 --> 00:16:34,386
[You Jung would be married by then?]
So I'd just be married in 10 years?

430
00:16:34,386 --> 00:16:36,179
Because I'd be the one to marry the fastest?

431
00:16:36,179 --> 00:16:38,333
Yeah, I guess.
It just came to me all of a sudden.

432
00:16:38,333 --> 00:16:41,366
Like, I wish we all ended up as neighbors.

433
00:16:41,366 --> 00:16:43,073
Oh, we did have that talk last time.

434
00:16:43,073 --> 00:16:45,057
[Friends you'd still want after 10 more years]
We'd babysit each other's kids.

435
00:16:45,057 --> 00:16:46,886
We could have vacations together.

436
00:16:46,886 --> 00:16:51,213
So by our 20th anniversary trip
we'd all be accompanied by babies?

437
00:16:51,213 --> 00:16:52,633
How old would we be by then?

438
00:16:52,633 --> 00:16:53,806
[10 years later, You Jung would be 37]
You Jung would be in her 30s.

439
00:16:53,806 --> 00:16:55,006
Mid 30s, actually.

440
00:16:55,006 --> 00:16:56,217
I'd be 46.

441
00:16:56,217 --> 00:16:57,241
Woah.

442
00:16:57,241 --> 00:16:59,679
I wish you longevity.

443
00:16:59,679 --> 00:17:01,993
[Heartfelt advice for the eldest]
You need to take good care of your health.

444
00:17:01,993 --> 00:17:03,699
Actually, look at the way he's dressed.

445
00:17:03,699 --> 00:17:06,359
[He looks like a typical middle-aged-hiker]
We might be riding Jin Young's boat today.

446
00:17:06,359 --> 00:17:08,130
[The boat we'll be rafting on may well be his]
We might be riding Jin Young's boat today.

447
00:17:08,130 --> 00:17:09,587
Wear these shades.

448
00:17:09,587 --> 00:17:11,987
[He looks like a rafting guide]
[Item added]

449
00:17:13,613 --> 00:17:16,386
[Boat captain core]
Oh, captain, captain!

450
00:17:16,386 --> 00:17:18,393
- It suits you. Captain.
- Captain Jin.

451
00:17:18,393 --> 00:17:19,990
That's hilarious.

452
00:17:19,990 --> 00:17:22,533
[Right on time, today's lunch has arrived]
Oh, thank you.

453
00:17:22,533 --> 00:17:24,406
Appreciate it.

454
00:17:24,406 --> 00:17:27,808
[The main dish, boneless short ribs,
presentable and pink]

455
00:17:27,808 --> 00:17:30,477
[Current time 10:30]
Grilling meat for breakfast. How luxurious.

456
00:17:30,477 --> 00:17:31,938
It looks so good.

457
00:17:32,759 --> 00:17:36,100
[The meat has already turned golden brown]
Looks so delicious. Salty and savory.

458
00:17:36,786 --> 00:17:38,176
[Full of plump octopus]
Wow.

459
00:17:38,176 --> 00:17:41,571
[Octopus on a griddle, looking tasty as ever]
The octopus looks so good.

460
00:17:41,571 --> 00:17:44,376
[And a crispy and moist potato pancake]
This is a lot of food!

461
00:17:44,376 --> 00:17:46,049
[Photos are obligatory even before a meal]
Let's take a photo.

462
00:17:46,049 --> 00:17:47,743
Everyone, look here.

463
00:17:47,743 --> 00:17:49,660
One, two, three.

464
00:17:49,660 --> 00:17:52,376
[First meal of the trip is a feast!]
Perfect.

465
00:17:52,376 --> 00:17:54,100
La la, looks so good!

466
00:17:54,100 --> 00:17:56,043
- Let's enjoy this food!
- Thank you for the meal!

467
00:17:56,043 --> 00:17:57,883
Let's hit it.

468
00:17:57,883 --> 00:18:00,583
[The short rib wins the first bite,
dipped in sauce]

469
00:18:01,296 --> 00:18:03,834
- Mm!
- Is it good?

470
00:18:04,529 --> 00:18:06,369
[Taste so good it awes you]

471
00:18:06,369 --> 00:18:08,083
Gangwon beef is the best beef.

472
00:18:08,083 --> 00:18:09,749
Is it that good?

473
00:18:09,749 --> 00:18:11,669
[Eldest Jin Young takes a bite]

474
00:18:11,669 --> 00:18:12,669
Wow.

475
00:18:14,056 --> 00:18:15,733
[Just as tasty for their first meal]
So good.

476
00:18:15,733 --> 00:18:16,783
It's really good.

477
00:18:16,783 --> 00:18:19,583
[Put some meat on some perilla leaves]

478
00:18:19,583 --> 00:18:24,563
[and take a well-balanced bite]

479
00:18:24,563 --> 00:18:28,116
[You Jung is having the time of her life]

480
00:18:28,116 --> 00:18:30,563
[Chomp]

481
00:18:30,563 --> 00:18:34,856
[Muk-Bo Gum binges on meat ssams as well]

482
00:18:34,856 --> 00:18:38,703
Do you remember the day
we did the full script reading?

483
00:18:38,703 --> 00:18:39,729
[Dong Yeon was a late recruit]
I wasn't there.

484
00:18:39,729 --> 00:18:41,423
Yeah, I remember. He wasn't there.

485
00:18:41,423 --> 00:18:43,043
I just remembered what I was wearing that day.

486
00:18:43,043 --> 00:18:44,809
No way! What were you wearing?

487
00:18:44,809 --> 00:18:46,416
A white shirt.

488
00:18:46,416 --> 00:18:47,769
I think I wore a white shirt, too.

489
00:18:47,769 --> 00:18:49,043
I was wearing white, too!

490
00:18:49,043 --> 00:18:51,043
Hey, I think I did, too.

491
00:18:51,876 --> 00:18:54,316
[They all wore white as if they'd planned it]

492
00:18:55,356 --> 00:18:57,736
Yeah, I was wearing white, too. At home.

493
00:18:59,129 --> 00:19:02,023
[Dong Yeon stayed true
to the dress code as well, it seems]

494
00:19:02,023 --> 00:19:04,099
I was in that phase at the time.

495
00:19:04,099 --> 00:19:06,123
[Original director of Love in the Moonlight]
I hated director Seong Yoon.

496
00:19:06,123 --> 00:19:07,296
Why?

497
00:19:07,296 --> 00:19:10,580
[They had worked together from Puberty Medley]
I'd already worked with him, so we were close.

498
00:19:10,580 --> 00:19:12,236
So I thought I'd get to audition
for 'Love in the Moonlight' as well.

499
00:19:12,236 --> 00:19:14,603
But he didn't call me in.

500
00:19:14,603 --> 00:19:17,776
So I gave him a call asking
why he didn't call me in.

501
00:19:17,776 --> 00:19:18,936
What did he say?

502
00:19:18,936 --> 00:19:21,487
"You don't need an audition, I know you."

503
00:19:21,487 --> 00:19:22,819
He said no.

504
00:19:22,819 --> 00:19:25,505
So I went straight to the office to audition.

505
00:19:25,505 --> 00:19:28,192
[That's how badly he wanted the role]

506
00:19:28,192 --> 00:19:31,512
I told him I wanted to play Byeong Yeon.

507
00:19:31,512 --> 00:19:33,463
[But he didn't get cast for the role]
But I still didn't get it.

508
00:19:33,463 --> 00:19:35,452
So I was cursing him at home.

509
00:19:35,452 --> 00:19:38,579
[Guess he wasn't in normal white clothes]
Yeah, in white mourning clothes, the full pack.

510
00:19:38,579 --> 00:19:39,646
And then...

511
00:19:39,646 --> 00:19:41,415
I took back all of the curses
I put on him once I got the part.

512
00:19:41,415 --> 00:19:44,012
[I took everything back since we became a team]
Reversed the curse.

513
00:19:44,012 --> 00:19:45,389
Oh, do you guys remember?

514
00:19:45,389 --> 00:19:47,873
I used to call everyone "uncle"
because I was so young,

515
00:19:47,873 --> 00:19:50,279
and I felt awkward having to say "oppa,"

516
00:19:50,279 --> 00:19:52,212
so I just didn't use it.

517
00:19:52,212 --> 00:19:55,425
I would just say "hyung," or just "mister."

518
00:19:55,425 --> 00:19:58,259
Remember I used to call you
Mr. Bo Gum and Mr. You Jung?

519
00:19:58,259 --> 00:20:00,785
But then, people wanted me to change it.

520
00:20:00,785 --> 00:20:03,620
They told me to call him Bo Gum oppa.

521
00:20:03,620 --> 00:20:07,074
So he became the only person
I'd ever use "oppa" to, at the time.

522
00:20:07,074 --> 00:20:08,616
Just what happened back then.

523
00:20:08,616 --> 00:20:10,525
- I'm honored.
- Except for my real brother, of course.

524
00:20:10,525 --> 00:20:13,232
[Bo Gum took the honor ten years ago]
That makes me kind of glad.

525
00:20:13,232 --> 00:20:15,203
I'm craving something like makgeolli.

526
00:20:15,203 --> 00:20:16,939
Let's grab some from the supermarket later.

527
00:20:16,939 --> 00:20:18,363
I'm on vacation mode today.

528
00:20:18,363 --> 00:20:20,679
- Oh, right. Of course.
- I'm going to get hammered today.

529
00:20:20,679 --> 00:20:22,032
[Shocked]

530
00:20:22,032 --> 00:20:24,572
[An unfathomable concept to Park, the nice kid]
Look at his face!

531
00:20:24,572 --> 00:20:27,339
Did you ever drink with us, You Jung?

532
00:20:27,339 --> 00:20:29,243
- We've drunk, yeah. Lots.
- That day...

533
00:20:29,243 --> 00:20:31,653
Did I not drink that day?
When the three of us met?

534
00:20:31,653 --> 00:20:33,761
There was that day where we went off the rails.

535
00:20:33,761 --> 00:20:35,833
In Yongsan, remember?

536
00:20:35,833 --> 00:20:37,437
Wasn't it a spontaneous thing?

537
00:20:37,437 --> 00:20:39,163
[Bo Gum, You Jung, and Dong Yeon showed up]
Yeah, it was. It was.

538
00:20:39,163 --> 00:20:41,016
But I think you contacted everyone here.

539
00:20:41,016 --> 00:20:42,587
- Yeah, I joined in late.
- And all of a sudden...

540
00:20:42,587 --> 00:20:45,169
- Bo Gum really let himself go that day.
- Right, I remember.

541
00:20:45,169 --> 00:20:48,343
He was begging us to go bar hopping.

542
00:20:48,343 --> 00:20:50,544
Yeah, we stayed out so late that night.

543
00:20:50,544 --> 00:20:54,675
I think that was the first time
I've ever stayed out that late.

544
00:20:54,675 --> 00:20:58,575
I think that was
the most you've ever drank, too.

545
00:20:58,575 --> 00:21:01,602
[The most Bo Gum has ever drunk is a pint]
Yeah, I had a full pint, right?

546
00:21:01,602 --> 00:21:05,275
What surprised me more was that there were
places still open at such an hour.

547
00:21:05,275 --> 00:21:06,726
[He didn't know about the Yongsan nightlife]
Bo Gum...

548
00:21:06,726 --> 00:21:08,910
- And you were...
- That's Yongsan to you.

549
00:21:08,910 --> 00:21:10,915
I'm never outside at those hours.

550
00:21:10,915 --> 00:21:14,862
Thank you for enjoying spending time with us.

551
00:21:14,862 --> 00:21:16,002
[New horizons...]
Of course I do.

552
00:21:16,002 --> 00:21:18,509
[are best explored with the Moonlight cast]
It was a historical moment, yes.

553
00:21:18,509 --> 00:21:21,362
We're going to need lots of strength
for the upcoming day and a half.

554
00:21:21,362 --> 00:21:24,344
[Bo Gum prepared gifts for everyone]
First off, have one of these.

555
00:21:24,344 --> 00:21:26,715
[Red ginseng extract for energy!]
Take these to re-energize.

556
00:21:26,715 --> 00:21:28,462
- Oh, it's 'Everytime'.
- Thank you!

557
00:21:28,462 --> 00:21:29,709
Thanks.

558
00:21:29,709 --> 00:21:31,802
Let's get our energy levels up and go rafting!

559
00:21:31,802 --> 00:21:33,455
Yes sir!

560
00:21:33,455 --> 00:21:35,455
[Power up!]

561
00:21:37,008 --> 00:21:40,192
I really like how easy and revitalizing it is.

562
00:21:40,192 --> 00:21:41,388
Now, let's go rafting!

563
00:21:41,388 --> 00:21:42,873
- Let's go!
- Off we go!

564
00:21:42,873 --> 00:21:46,620
[Full bellies call for a refreshing rafting!]
- Go, go! - Thank you for the amazing meal!

565
00:21:48,115 --> 00:21:50,622
[Clear skies,]
The weather is perfect.

566
00:21:50,622 --> 00:21:52,035
What kind of tree is that?

567
00:21:52,035 --> 00:21:53,059
[and pretty flowers]
Oh, how pretty!

568
00:21:53,059 --> 00:21:54,475
It's a Rose of Sharon.

569
00:21:54,475 --> 00:21:56,415
- Oh, really?
- Wow!

570
00:21:56,415 --> 00:21:59,219
Hey, what's that over there?
I want to go play there.

571
00:21:59,219 --> 00:22:00,255
I want to dive in!

572
00:22:00,255 --> 00:22:04,529
[The river is finally in sight]

573
00:22:04,529 --> 00:22:05,815
Oh, look! Life vests.

574
00:22:05,815 --> 00:22:08,008
[Nervous]
Would this be enough for you?

575
00:22:08,008 --> 00:22:09,539
[The moment of doom approaches]
Or do you need them to be thicker?

576
00:22:09,539 --> 00:22:11,602
- No, not at all. I'm fine...
- Uh, yes, you do.

577
00:22:11,602 --> 00:22:13,906
[Arrived at last!]
Oh, you're still scared, aren't you?

578
00:22:13,906 --> 00:22:15,848
I've never done anything like this before.

579
00:22:15,848 --> 00:22:17,299
Thank you!

580
00:22:17,299 --> 00:22:19,835
- Hello!
- Good morning!

581
00:22:19,835 --> 00:22:23,042
I'll be guiding the five of you for the day.

582
00:22:23,042 --> 00:22:25,386
- Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you.

583
00:22:25,386 --> 00:22:27,502
Please, take special care of this one.

584
00:22:27,502 --> 00:22:28,922
[Scaredy-cat(35): scared of water]
What, me?

585
00:22:28,922 --> 00:22:32,762
[Life vests on first and foremost]
Before we go, put on the life vests behind you.

586
00:22:32,762 --> 00:22:35,312
So, about the course that we'll be taking...

587
00:22:35,312 --> 00:22:38,070
[Checking the difficulty for the eldest baby]
How "thrilling" would it be?

588
00:22:38,070 --> 00:22:40,422
- On a scale from one to ten?
- Yeah, on a scale to ten.

589
00:22:40,422 --> 00:22:42,816
[A seven or eight out of ten!]
Around seven or eight.

590
00:22:42,816 --> 00:22:45,336
[Shocked]
Seven or eight.

591
00:22:45,336 --> 00:22:48,029
[Go on ahead, guys... I'll just see myself out]

592
00:22:48,029 --> 00:22:49,329
[Taking a ride to the boarding point]
Excuse me.

593
00:22:49,329 --> 00:22:51,665
- Hi.
- Hello.

594
00:22:51,665 --> 00:22:53,869
You have such broad shoulders.

595
00:22:54,822 --> 00:22:56,929
Wow, you look totally ripped right now.

596
00:22:57,896 --> 00:23:00,628
Sir, how is Hongcheon river this year?

597
00:23:00,628 --> 00:23:01,575
Will we fall in the water?

598
00:23:01,575 --> 00:23:03,436
How long is the ride?

599
00:23:03,436 --> 00:23:04,460
About one and a half hours.

600
00:23:04,460 --> 00:23:05,949
[More excitement just means more questions]

601
00:23:05,949 --> 00:23:09,613
[The rafting site
is getting closer by the minute]

602
00:23:09,613 --> 00:23:11,417
Wait, the river is really rapid!

603
00:23:11,417 --> 00:23:12,441
Where? Let me see!

604
00:23:12,441 --> 00:23:14,402
[The current appears to be rapid]
Yeah, it's flowing fast!

605
00:23:14,402 --> 00:23:17,800
The current is faster than expected!

606
00:23:17,800 --> 00:23:21,150
Mr. Jin Young's thoughts
must be racing right now.

607
00:23:22,019 --> 00:23:23,463
[Jin Young's race against fate has also begun]
It'll be fine.

608
00:23:23,463 --> 00:23:25,606
We're here.

609
00:23:25,606 --> 00:23:28,114
- Thank you.
- Thanks for the ride!

610
00:23:28,806 --> 00:23:32,126
Wow! This looks like so much fun!

611
00:23:32,126 --> 00:23:33,983
[Hongcheon river rafting]

612
00:23:34,799 --> 00:23:38,079
[Boating along the twisting river...]

613
00:23:38,753 --> 00:23:40,793
[Hongcheon's famed water sports activity]

614
00:23:41,379 --> 00:23:44,893
[Ten years ago, Ra On fell from a boat...]

615
00:23:46,288 --> 00:23:47,928
Y-your highness!

616
00:23:48,546 --> 00:23:53,887
[and Lee Yeong leaped to the rescue]
Your highness!

617
00:23:54,613 --> 00:23:56,613
[As this is a 10th anniversary trip...]

618
00:23:57,566 --> 00:24:01,199
[all five friends will be jumping in
without a care in the world!]

619
00:24:01,993 --> 00:24:05,573
[The episode was filmed under surveillance
of experts, following safety rules]

620
00:24:06,406 --> 00:24:09,646
[The Moonlight Five are on board!]
Strap your foot in, and let the other one hang.

621
00:24:09,646 --> 00:24:11,133
[Ship Hongcheon river Moonlight sets sail!]
Let's start.

622
00:24:11,133 --> 00:24:13,083
- Yes, sir.
- Let's go catch a shark!

623
00:24:13,083 --> 00:24:16,917
Let's see if your voice is loud enough,
and if you row well enough!

624
00:24:16,917 --> 00:24:18,907
- Yes, sir!
- Forward! One, two!

625
00:24:18,907 --> 00:24:20,745
- Three, four!
- Three, four!

626
00:24:20,745 --> 00:24:22,553
- One, two!
- Three, four!

627
00:24:22,553 --> 00:24:23,637
[Still has a long way to row]
One, two!

628
00:24:23,637 --> 00:24:25,646
- Three, four!
- One, two!

629
00:24:25,646 --> 00:24:27,570
- Three, four!
- And cease.

630
00:24:27,570 --> 00:24:29,507
When I say "cease,"
the paddles return to your knees.

631
00:24:29,507 --> 00:24:31,279
- On my knees.
- On my knees!

632
00:24:31,279 --> 00:24:34,233
- Why am I getting a preview of the army life?
- Take a knee!

633
00:24:34,233 --> 00:24:37,226
[Fun fact: Dong Yeon is to be enlisted
in three weeks from this moment]

634
00:24:37,226 --> 00:24:39,933
On the left! Your voice was too small.

635
00:24:39,933 --> 00:24:41,550
[You three! Louder!]
The left side was being too quiet, right?

636
00:24:41,550 --> 00:24:42,967
- The left side? Yeah!
- Yes!

637
00:24:42,967 --> 00:24:44,806
- They weren't loud enough.
- Boo!

638
00:24:44,806 --> 00:24:47,018
- Boo! Boo!
- Boo!

639
00:24:47,018 --> 00:24:50,046
[Soo Bin, report!]
You hear that, Soo Bin?

640
00:24:50,046 --> 00:24:52,103
[Private Herbivore's just sunshine and daisies]
Do you want to take a dip first?

641
00:24:52,103 --> 00:24:53,274
Oh, no, no, we're fine.

642
00:24:53,274 --> 00:24:57,958
Now, the third person on the left side
will give us a good chant!

643
00:24:57,958 --> 00:24:59,777
[Jin Young's chant]
- Oh, me? - So, that's you, right there.

644
00:24:59,777 --> 00:25:01,693
It goes "one, two," and we're off!

645
00:25:01,693 --> 00:25:02,717
[Squad on a mission!]
One, two!

646
00:25:02,717 --> 00:25:03,960
- Three, four!
- One, two!

647
00:25:03,960 --> 00:25:04,984
[Synchronized rowing at its best]
Three, four!

648
00:25:04,984 --> 00:25:06,346
- One, two!
- Three, four!

649
00:25:06,346 --> 00:25:07,826
- One, two...
- Three, four!

650
00:25:07,826 --> 00:25:09,286
- One, two!
- Three, four!

651
00:25:09,286 --> 00:25:10,990
- One, two!
- Cease!

652
00:25:10,990 --> 00:25:12,681
Now, moving on to the person right in front.

653
00:25:12,681 --> 00:25:15,726
[The smaller the voice, the faster the dive]
The one with the smallest voice dives first.

654
00:25:15,726 --> 00:25:17,646
Let's go, number two.

655
00:25:17,646 --> 00:25:19,083
- One! Two!
- Three, four!

656
00:25:19,083 --> 00:25:20,574
- One, two!
- Three, four!

657
00:25:20,574 --> 00:25:22,231
- One! Two!
- Three, four!

658
00:25:22,231 --> 00:25:23,693
[The cue to row is on "three, four"...]
Three, four!

659
00:25:23,693 --> 00:25:24,757
- One! Two!
- Three, four!

660
00:25:24,757 --> 00:25:25,786
[Falter]
One! Two!

661
00:25:25,786 --> 00:25:27,154
Three, four!

662
00:25:27,154 --> 00:25:28,422
Her paddling is off!

663
00:25:28,422 --> 00:25:30,190
[Just loud and wrong...]
She's paddling at "one, two!"

664
00:25:30,190 --> 00:25:32,479
[our dear Private Herbivore]
The rhythm is awful!

665
00:25:32,479 --> 00:25:35,486
- Totally wrong...
- Just give me one more chance!

666
00:25:35,486 --> 00:25:37,119
Okay, let's go!

667
00:25:37,119 --> 00:25:38,403
I don't think another chance
will make any difference.

668
00:25:38,403 --> 00:25:40,394
- No, sir! I can do it, sir!
- Let's go!

669
00:25:40,394 --> 00:25:41,938
- One! Two!
- Three, four!

670
00:25:41,938 --> 00:25:43,426
- One! Two!
- Three, four.

671
00:25:43,426 --> 00:25:44,857
- One, two!
- Three, four!

672
00:25:44,857 --> 00:25:45,881
[She's laughing, too]
One, two...

673
00:25:45,881 --> 00:25:47,086
- Three, four!
- One! Two!

674
00:25:47,086 --> 00:25:48,319
- Three, four!
- Cease.

675
00:25:48,319 --> 00:25:51,706
I heard you well enough. Now, moving on!

676
00:25:51,706 --> 00:25:53,377
- One! Two!
- Three, four!

677
00:25:53,377 --> 00:25:54,934
- One! Two!
- Three, four!

678
00:25:54,934 --> 00:25:56,546
[Loud and ringing]
One! Two!

679
00:25:56,546 --> 00:25:58,093
- One! Two!
- Three, four!

680
00:25:58,093 --> 00:25:59,337
- One! Two!
- Three, four!

681
00:25:59,337 --> 00:26:01,207
- Is this all you've got, Marine?
- Three, four!

682
00:26:01,207 --> 00:26:02,846
[Navy force activated]
- One! Two! - Three, four!

683
00:26:02,846 --> 00:26:04,619
- One! Two!
- Three, four!

684
00:26:04,619 --> 00:26:05,643
One-two!

685
00:26:05,643 --> 00:26:06,653
[Private Gwak on the frontier]
Three, four!

686
00:26:06,653 --> 00:26:08,237
- One-two!
- Three, four!

687
00:26:08,237 --> 00:26:09,261
[Rowing at a right angle]
One-two!

688
00:26:09,261 --> 00:26:10,645
- Three, four!
- One-two!

689
00:26:10,645 --> 00:26:11,669
Three, four!

690
00:26:11,669 --> 00:26:12,946
[Sergeant Kim is here!]
Sea! Waves!

691
00:26:12,946 --> 00:26:14,757
- Sea! Waves!
- Three, four!

692
00:26:14,757 --> 00:26:16,038
Sea! Waves!

693
00:26:16,038 --> 00:26:17,053
[The short-timer sergeant is the loudest]
Three, four!

694
00:26:17,053 --> 00:26:18,917
- Sea! Waves!
- Three, four!

695
00:26:18,917 --> 00:26:21,854
Oof, my throat is so sore.
How am I going to reenact the show now?

696
00:26:21,854 --> 00:26:23,453
Yeah, a sore throat is no joke.

697
00:26:23,453 --> 00:26:25,583
[Team A: Bo Gum, Soo Bin, Jin Young]
The left side is team A,

698
00:26:25,583 --> 00:26:27,607
[Team B: Dong Yeon, You Jung]
and on the right is team B.

699
00:26:27,607 --> 00:26:32,209
From now on, both teams A and B
will climb onto the rail.

700
00:26:32,209 --> 00:26:33,840
- The rail?
- Railing? Oh, here?

701
00:26:33,840 --> 00:26:36,066
Yes, now rise!

702
00:26:36,066 --> 00:26:37,090
[Suddenly excited]
I think we're fighting!

703
00:26:37,090 --> 00:26:38,119
No way!

704
00:26:38,119 --> 00:26:39,639
One, two, three.

705
00:26:39,639 --> 00:26:40,639
Wait!

706
00:26:40,639 --> 00:26:42,697
[It's hard just standing upright]
You can hold onto me.

707
00:26:42,697 --> 00:26:43,841
You can hold onto me.

708
00:26:43,841 --> 00:26:46,045
[Grasp]
Oh, my gosh!

709
00:26:46,045 --> 00:26:47,322
[Team B is steady and successful]
How do I climb on top?

710
00:26:47,322 --> 00:26:49,493
That's it, yeah.

711
00:26:49,493 --> 00:26:51,337
Watch out for the center.

712
00:26:51,337 --> 00:26:53,781
[Making a ruckus]
No, don't let go of me!

713
00:26:53,781 --> 00:26:55,033
You'll need to let go.

714
00:26:55,033 --> 00:26:56,493
[Team A isn't doing so hot]
But sir!

715
00:26:56,493 --> 00:26:57,933
If you want stability,
just hold on to those two.

716
00:26:57,933 --> 00:26:59,086
That's true.

717
00:26:59,086 --> 00:27:01,214
Shoulder to shoulder! Go shoulder to shoulder.

718
00:27:01,214 --> 00:27:04,433
Shoulder to shoul-der!

719
00:27:04,433 --> 00:27:06,759
One of the teams is going to fall.

720
00:27:06,759 --> 00:27:08,179
[One of the teams will fall?]
Just one team.

721
00:27:08,179 --> 00:27:10,113
Now, team A will slowly crouch down.

722
00:27:10,113 --> 00:27:11,963
- Team A, crouching...
- Crouching...

723
00:27:11,963 --> 00:27:15,199
- And as they rise back up, team B will crouch.
- Okay.

724
00:27:15,199 --> 00:27:17,519
We'll repeat this until one of you falls.

725
00:27:17,519 --> 00:27:19,113
Let's go! One!

726
00:27:19,113 --> 00:27:21,519
[Wobble wobble]
Two!

727
00:27:23,919 --> 00:27:25,353
- Hey, wait.
- Two!

728
00:27:25,353 --> 00:27:28,117
[Teetering and tottering...]

729
00:27:28,117 --> 00:27:31,094
[and then she gives a deep bow!]

730
00:27:31,094 --> 00:27:32,118
No, don't give a deep bow!

731
00:27:32,118 --> 00:27:33,605
[Tumble]
What's up with that?

732
00:27:33,605 --> 00:27:35,549
Do it again, come on. Let's redo that.

733
00:27:35,549 --> 00:27:38,071
Sir, y-you almost threw me overboard!

734
00:27:38,986 --> 00:27:41,399
[Just full of joy and whimsy]

735
00:27:41,399 --> 00:27:43,253
[Herbivore down!]
You okay?

736
00:27:43,253 --> 00:27:45,013
You have to get back up.

737
00:27:45,013 --> 00:27:46,699
Let's try again.

738
00:27:46,699 --> 00:27:48,179
- Until someone falls in.
- Wait, wait.

739
00:27:48,179 --> 00:27:49,346
Is this right?

740
00:27:49,346 --> 00:27:51,405
Take it slow. Try to stand.

741
00:27:51,405 --> 00:27:53,293
[Back on the edge]
Slow and steady.

742
00:27:53,293 --> 00:27:55,619
- You can grab onto me.
- You go first.

743
00:27:55,619 --> 00:27:58,163
[The never-ending seesaw starts again]
Let's start from the top. Team A, squat.

744
00:27:58,163 --> 00:27:59,894
- Crouch...
- Again, now, one!

745
00:27:59,894 --> 00:28:00,958
- One...
- Two!

746
00:28:00,958 --> 00:28:01,982
- Two...
- One!

747
00:28:01,982 --> 00:28:03,973
[The boat wobbles again]
One, two!

748
00:28:03,973 --> 00:28:06,119
- One, two!
- One, two!

749
00:28:11,629 --> 00:28:13,415
[Good-bye]

750
00:28:17,975 --> 00:28:21,182
[The honor of taking the first dip
goes to team A]

751
00:28:25,309 --> 00:28:28,142
[Ugh!]

752
00:28:28,782 --> 00:28:30,036
[Nice play!]

753
00:28:30,036 --> 00:28:33,182
We did it! We survived!

754
00:28:33,182 --> 00:28:35,642
[Sputter sputter]

755
00:28:35,642 --> 00:28:38,255
Toodles, stragglers!

756
00:28:38,255 --> 00:28:40,066
[The soggy stragglers]
We're leaving you!

757
00:28:40,066 --> 00:28:41,909
We're leaving without you!

758
00:28:41,909 --> 00:28:43,729
Are you alright?

759
00:28:43,729 --> 00:28:45,442
[Not at all, actually...]

760
00:28:45,442 --> 00:28:46,694
Oh, thank you.

761
00:28:46,694 --> 00:28:48,161
- Oh, it got in my mouth.
- I really tried...

762
00:28:48,161 --> 00:28:50,469
[The stragglers are back on board]

763
00:28:50,469 --> 00:28:52,562
[Bo Gum swiftly climbs back on]
Wait, is that yours?

764
00:28:52,562 --> 00:28:53,686
[You Jung tries to help Soo Bin up]
Turn your back to me.

765
00:28:53,686 --> 00:28:54,948
Like this?

766
00:28:56,496 --> 00:28:59,943
Ow, my crotch!

767
00:29:00,875 --> 00:29:03,029
I'm sorry, I'm sorry!

768
00:29:03,029 --> 00:29:05,622
[The life vest straps go on the legs]
I forgot the strap went on the legs.

769
00:29:05,622 --> 00:29:07,635
- Again, again.
- Wouldn't it hurt?

770
00:29:07,635 --> 00:29:08,882
No, I'll just hold it.

771
00:29:08,882 --> 00:29:10,182
Oh, okay.

772
00:29:10,182 --> 00:29:11,335
[Rushing to help]
Won't it hurt?

773
00:29:11,335 --> 00:29:13,453
Yeah, she's holding it. One, two, three!

774
00:29:15,549 --> 00:29:17,562
[A real big catch comes with a wail]
It's like we caught a fish.

775
00:29:17,562 --> 00:29:19,322
Just hauling her up like a catch.

776
00:29:19,322 --> 00:29:20,715
[Guys, what about me?]

777
00:29:27,542 --> 00:29:30,375
[Team A, back on board screaming]

778
00:29:30,375 --> 00:29:31,531
Do we get back into position?

779
00:29:31,531 --> 00:29:33,682
- Yes, back in position.
- Yes, sir.

780
00:29:33,682 --> 00:29:35,093
Okay, then. Again...

781
00:29:35,093 --> 00:29:36,789
[Moving forward!]
Forward!

782
00:29:36,789 --> 00:29:38,059
Louder, one, two!

783
00:29:38,059 --> 00:29:39,690
- Three! Four!
- One, two!

784
00:29:39,690 --> 00:29:41,289
- Three, four!
- One! Two!

785
00:29:41,289 --> 00:29:42,302
[Morales are high]
Three, four!

786
00:29:42,302 --> 00:29:43,453
- One, two!
- Three, four!

787
00:29:43,453 --> 00:29:44,709
- One-two!
- Three-four!

788
00:29:44,709 --> 00:29:45,879
- One-two!
- Three, four!

789
00:29:45,879 --> 00:29:47,135
[Splish splash]
- One, two! - Three, four!

790
00:29:47,135 --> 00:29:48,309
- One-two!
- Three-four!

791
00:29:48,309 --> 00:29:49,449
- One, two!
- Three, four!

792
00:29:49,449 --> 00:29:50,483
- One-two!
- Three, four!

793
00:29:50,483 --> 00:29:51,543
[Private Gwak of pure passion]
- One, two! - Three! Four!

794
00:29:51,543 --> 00:29:52,574
- One-two!
- Three-four!

795
00:29:52,574 --> 00:29:53,918
- One, two!
- Three, four!

796
00:29:53,918 --> 00:29:54,969
And cease!

797
00:29:54,969 --> 00:29:55,975
Hey, excuse me.

798
00:29:55,975 --> 00:29:57,849
Could you not splash me with water, please?

799
00:29:57,849 --> 00:29:59,959
[Private Gwak is too passionate]
You were practically shoveling it onto me.

800
00:29:59,959 --> 00:30:01,421
I got too eager.

801
00:30:01,421 --> 00:30:03,389
- I mean, I don't want to be the one to dive.
- That's so funny.

802
00:30:03,389 --> 00:30:05,459
The right-side team has only two people,
but you're way better than the left.

803
00:30:05,459 --> 00:30:06,657
You guys are good at rowing.

804
00:30:06,657 --> 00:30:07,669
We are, aren't we?

805
00:30:07,669 --> 00:30:09,889
- Boo!
- Boo-oo!

806
00:30:09,889 --> 00:30:11,554
The three seniors.

807
00:30:11,554 --> 00:30:13,578
The three seniors?

808
00:30:13,578 --> 00:30:15,109
[Senior #1(33), #2(32), #3(35)]

809
00:30:15,109 --> 00:30:16,795
[Being in your 30s is considered old here]
We can't even deny it, it's so frustrating.

810
00:30:16,795 --> 00:30:19,297
- Forward! One, two!
- Three, four!

811
00:30:19,297 --> 00:30:21,948
[The energetic 20-year-olds...]
- One, two! - Three, four!

812
00:30:21,948 --> 00:30:24,355
[and the 30s, trying their best]
- One, two! - Three, four!

813
00:30:24,355 --> 00:30:25,459
- Cease!
- Cease.

814
00:30:25,459 --> 00:30:27,230
On my knees.

815
00:30:27,230 --> 00:30:29,069
Do you like diving?

816
00:30:29,069 --> 00:30:31,153
- What?
- Diving. Do you like to dive?

817
00:30:31,153 --> 00:30:32,517
Uh, no?

818
00:30:32,517 --> 00:30:35,669
Up ahead, 12 o'clock, you see all those boats?

819
00:30:35,669 --> 00:30:36,746
- Yes.
- That tower of boats?

820
00:30:36,746 --> 00:30:38,437
- We're going to dive from it.
- Wow!

821
00:30:38,437 --> 00:30:39,927
We can dive? Oh, wow.

822
00:30:39,927 --> 00:30:41,602
What?

823
00:30:41,602 --> 00:30:44,682
[In the middle of the Hongcheon river...]

824
00:30:45,295 --> 00:30:48,809
[is a thrilling diving spot!]
[Safety guards]

825
00:30:49,455 --> 00:30:50,759
Oh, it's a stack of boats?

826
00:30:50,759 --> 00:30:53,109
Yes, that's the highest we can stack them.

827
00:30:53,109 --> 00:30:54,619
Is that about three meters high?

828
00:30:54,619 --> 00:30:57,402
[It's about three meters tall]
Almost, yeah.

829
00:30:57,402 --> 00:30:59,215
No way I can jump from that.

830
00:30:59,215 --> 00:31:01,522
What? That's nothing!

831
00:31:01,522 --> 00:31:02,809
[The episode was filmed under surveillance...]
Put the paddles away in the center,

832
00:31:02,809 --> 00:31:04,835
[of experts, following safety rules]
and slowly get off the boat.

833
00:31:04,835 --> 00:31:06,139
Hello, everyone.

834
00:31:06,139 --> 00:31:08,777
The one with the loudest voice...

835
00:31:08,777 --> 00:31:10,142
[First up is Bo Gum]
will go first.

836
00:31:10,142 --> 00:31:11,705
- Oh, first?
- Ah, well.

837
00:31:12,642 --> 00:31:15,135
- Stand in front of me.
- Oh, this looks fun!

838
00:31:15,135 --> 00:31:16,402
Forward.

839
00:31:16,402 --> 00:31:18,046
[Heart racing]
Jump far out, okay?

840
00:31:18,046 --> 00:31:19,451
I'm going to do it.

841
00:31:26,209 --> 00:31:29,262
[A running start followed by a cool jump]

842
00:31:35,949 --> 00:31:41,749
[His diving form is just as good
as when he dived to save Ra On]

843
00:31:45,182 --> 00:31:48,609
[President Park makes a great starting dive]

844
00:31:49,449 --> 00:31:50,842
[Maximum refreshment]

845
00:31:50,842 --> 00:31:52,686
It's so much fun!

846
00:31:52,686 --> 00:31:55,169
[You Jung is the next diver]
Next up!

847
00:31:55,169 --> 00:31:58,825
[Leaping and pouncing]
Take it easy.

848
00:32:00,009 --> 00:32:02,915
She's like a little kid.

849
00:32:02,915 --> 00:32:04,830
Like an excited kid.

850
00:32:05,762 --> 00:32:09,249
[Little You Jung has no fear!]

851
00:32:10,402 --> 00:32:12,882
Just aim for the farthest jump you can do.

852
00:32:12,882 --> 00:32:13,946
Far?

853
00:32:13,946 --> 00:32:16,155
Yeah, jump as far as you can.

854
00:32:22,202 --> 00:32:24,495
[Not a glimpse of hesitation to be found]

855
00:32:25,942 --> 00:32:29,709
[Unlike when she was a eunuch,
helplessly drowning in water...]

856
00:32:31,722 --> 00:32:35,522
[You Jung is enjoying her refreshing dive!]

857
00:32:35,522 --> 00:32:37,322
Oh, it's so cold!

858
00:32:37,322 --> 00:32:39,869
[While You Jung is enjoying her swim...]

859
00:32:39,869 --> 00:32:41,935
[Private Gwak has bravely made his climb]
- Go, Gwak Dong Yeon!

860
00:32:41,935 --> 00:32:43,609
Oh, so cool!

861
00:32:48,615 --> 00:32:51,015
[Private Gwak does a flip!]

862
00:32:56,236 --> 00:32:58,755
- That's awesome!
- That was so cool!

863
00:32:58,755 --> 00:33:00,709
- Seriously, that was amazing.
- Wow, what was that?

864
00:33:00,709 --> 00:33:03,675
[Feeling awesome]

865
00:33:03,675 --> 00:33:05,413
How did you do that?

866
00:33:05,413 --> 00:33:07,255
Just do a flip.

867
00:33:07,255 --> 00:33:09,462
Like, flip out!

868
00:33:09,462 --> 00:33:11,762
[The prince tries his hand at it, too]
You can do it!

869
00:33:11,762 --> 00:33:12,972
Come on!

870
00:33:15,795 --> 00:33:16,909
What was that?

871
00:33:17,609 --> 00:33:19,722
[Took a wrong step]

872
00:33:20,749 --> 00:33:23,102
[Something seems off]

873
00:33:23,102 --> 00:33:25,442
[Just ended up like some guy
who fell by accident]

874
00:33:26,151 --> 00:33:29,322
[The prince turns out to be a great jester]

875
00:33:29,322 --> 00:33:30,633
My knees folded weird...

876
00:33:30,633 --> 00:33:32,182
[Cackles]

877
00:33:32,182 --> 00:33:34,206
That's just falling over forward, no?

878
00:33:34,206 --> 00:33:36,089
Did you get a good look at the water?

879
00:33:36,089 --> 00:33:38,109
[Nod nod]

880
00:33:38,109 --> 00:33:40,070
Next!

881
00:33:40,070 --> 00:33:43,022
[All that's left are Soo Bin and Jin Young]
Next!

882
00:33:43,022 --> 00:33:45,895
Why are you both shying away?

883
00:33:45,895 --> 00:33:46,933
- Are you going to?
- It's fun!

884
00:33:46,933 --> 00:33:48,195
Can I just not jump?

885
00:33:48,195 --> 00:33:49,709
[Whispers of the Devil]
You don't have to, but just climb up here.

886
00:33:49,709 --> 00:33:51,439
It's really fun, just try!

887
00:33:51,439 --> 00:33:53,006
I still have to climb up there?

888
00:33:54,431 --> 00:33:56,149
[Soo Bin musters up the courage and climbs up]

889
00:33:56,149 --> 00:33:57,715
It's hot, so be careful.

890
00:34:00,545 --> 00:34:02,682
Oh, no, this won't work.

891
00:34:02,682 --> 00:34:05,209
Soo Bin, trust me, it's not scary at all.

892
00:34:05,209 --> 00:34:06,914
You can't come back down anyway.

893
00:34:06,914 --> 00:34:09,455
- I want to go back down.
- You can't!

894
00:34:09,455 --> 00:34:11,029
[Soo Bin is already
past the point of no return]

895
00:34:11,029 --> 00:34:12,049
Yeah, no way back.

896
00:34:12,049 --> 00:34:13,942
Just scooch on over to the edge, come on.

897
00:34:13,942 --> 00:34:14,993
[Pins and needles]
Just to the edge.

898
00:34:14,993 --> 00:34:18,442
And now, from there,
it's safest to jump as far as you can. Go on.

899
00:34:18,442 --> 00:34:19,579
[Glance]

900
00:34:19,579 --> 00:34:21,377
[Tremble tremble]

901
00:34:21,377 --> 00:34:22,975
Oh, her legs are shaking!

902
00:34:22,975 --> 00:34:24,102
It's alright!

903
00:34:24,102 --> 00:34:25,518
Go, Chae Soo Bin!

904
00:34:26,242 --> 00:34:27,266
Far, jump far!

905
00:34:27,266 --> 00:34:29,782
[Up and down, up and down]
Come on!

906
00:34:29,782 --> 00:34:30,816
Eyes forward.

907
00:34:32,529 --> 00:34:35,015
I-I can't do it!

908
00:34:35,015 --> 00:34:36,649
It's scarier to climb down.

909
00:34:36,649 --> 00:34:38,913
[Dr. Oh Eun Young's solution]
Push her. Push her! Safely.

910
00:34:38,913 --> 00:34:39,937
[Rejected]
No way!

911
00:34:39,937 --> 00:34:41,421
Oh, can I push her?

912
00:34:41,421 --> 00:34:43,178
- No!
- If you don't jump in five seconds,

913
00:34:43,178 --> 00:34:44,982
I'll push you off. Five...

914
00:34:44,982 --> 00:34:46,009
Four...

915
00:34:46,009 --> 00:34:48,314
[I have to jump before I get pushed!]
Five... Four... Three...

916
00:34:48,314 --> 00:34:50,308
[You can do it, Soo Bin!]
Four... Three... Two...

917
00:34:53,495 --> 00:34:54,835
[With a sharp yelp...]

918
00:34:55,862 --> 00:34:57,475
Two...

919
00:34:57,475 --> 00:35:02,435
[The herbivore jumps in the water!]

920
00:35:03,722 --> 00:35:05,207
[Pop!]

921
00:35:05,207 --> 00:35:07,435
[Turns out, she's aquatic as well]

922
00:35:07,435 --> 00:35:09,969
[Good job, Chae Soo Bin!]

923
00:35:09,969 --> 00:35:13,075
- It worked.
- She jumped as soon as he said he'd push her.

924
00:35:13,075 --> 00:35:15,035
[With Soo Bin's success,
the air is thick with excitement]

925
00:35:15,035 --> 00:35:16,762
- What happened?
- Your hair!

926
00:35:19,602 --> 00:35:21,173
[Only one who isn't so jolly]

927
00:35:21,173 --> 00:35:22,629
You can do it!

928
00:35:24,082 --> 00:35:27,346
[The eldest was even scared of rafting]
<i>Rafting won't get you wet or anything, right?</i>

929
00:35:27,346 --> 00:35:28,542
<i>- Of course you'll get wet.
- Yeah, you will.</i>

930
00:35:28,542 --> 00:35:29,542
<i>Why?</i>

931
00:35:30,449 --> 00:35:34,942
[The youngsters have already
jumped with no fear at all...]

932
00:35:37,309 --> 00:35:39,775
[Shaking and trembling]

933
00:35:39,775 --> 00:35:41,775
[He'd sometimes laugh along...]

934
00:35:43,949 --> 00:35:46,842
[and he'd sigh...]

935
00:35:47,489 --> 00:35:50,802
[but now he's on the diving board!]
Don't worry.

936
00:35:50,802 --> 00:35:52,298
You can do it!

937
00:35:52,929 --> 00:35:55,595
W-wait a minute. Just wait.

938
00:35:55,595 --> 00:35:56,753
[His legs have gone weak already]
Get up.

939
00:35:56,753 --> 00:35:57,753
Ow, it's hot.

940
00:35:58,502 --> 00:36:00,235
It's fun, see? Be confident!

941
00:36:00,235 --> 00:36:02,139
[Isn't even listening]
No, wait...

942
00:36:02,139 --> 00:36:03,269
Wait, wait. This...

943
00:36:03,269 --> 00:36:05,099
[This is way too tall for him to handle]
This is hard.

944
00:36:05,099 --> 00:36:06,877
- Come on.
- You can do this!

945
00:36:06,877 --> 00:36:09,441
Big brother! Eldest brother!

946
00:36:09,441 --> 00:36:10,769
Show us a cool trick!

947
00:36:10,769 --> 00:36:12,769
Let me breathe, okay?

948
00:36:13,495 --> 00:36:14,495
He's adorable.

949
00:36:15,629 --> 00:36:17,122
[Heavy is the burden of being the eldest]
Sure, breathe in deep.

950
00:36:17,122 --> 00:36:18,402
Cute!

951
00:36:18,402 --> 00:36:19,466
Should I do the countdown for him, too?

952
00:36:19,466 --> 00:36:20,515
- Oh, no, no, no, no.
- Yes!

953
00:36:20,515 --> 00:36:21,539
- Five!
- Alright, alright!

954
00:36:21,539 --> 00:36:22,549
[Guys, please, calm down]
Four!

955
00:36:22,549 --> 00:36:24,662
I-I need to do my breathing exercise.

956
00:36:24,662 --> 00:36:26,179
[What a cutie.]

957
00:36:26,179 --> 00:36:27,179
Okay, I'm going.

958
00:36:29,022 --> 00:36:33,547
[There's nowhere else to run...]

959
00:36:33,547 --> 00:36:36,529
[The little ones are watching me!]
<i>Eldest brother! Show us a cool trick!</i>

960
00:36:37,995 --> 00:36:40,802
[I am the eldest of the Moonlight cast!]

961
00:36:45,502 --> 00:36:50,302
[He makes a beautiful dive
by overcoming his fear!]

962
00:36:55,198 --> 00:36:58,451
[The eldest could show courage
thanks to his younger peers' encouragement]

963
00:36:59,778 --> 00:37:01,491
[Tries to swim]

964
00:37:02,898 --> 00:37:05,605
[While the eldest is proud of himself...]

965
00:37:08,178 --> 00:37:11,945
[Bo Gum, You Jung and Dong Yeon
have all climbed to the top again]

966
00:37:12,541 --> 00:37:13,731
[The three friends
had so much chemistry ten years ago]

967
00:37:13,731 --> 00:37:15,715
- Grueling training...
- I'd hope so.

968
00:37:15,715 --> 00:37:17,091
Scooch forward a little more.

969
00:37:17,091 --> 00:37:18,595
[The Jahyeondang Three are diving together]
Yes, forward.

970
00:37:18,595 --> 00:37:21,267
All at once. One, two, three!

971
00:37:25,085 --> 00:37:28,051
[The Jahyeondang Three soars freely]

972
00:37:31,548 --> 00:37:34,308
[A three-person jump makes thrice the thrill!]

973
00:37:35,515 --> 00:37:38,281
[A group dive makes you laugh]

974
00:37:38,281 --> 00:37:42,515
[After a successful dive...]

975
00:37:42,515 --> 00:37:45,293
We'll head straight to the endpoint now.

976
00:37:45,293 --> 00:37:46,961
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir.

977
00:37:46,961 --> 00:37:51,401
[Swimming towards the end point]

978
00:37:51,401 --> 00:37:54,155
Let's race to see who's the fastest swimmer!

979
00:37:54,155 --> 00:37:55,219
Sounds good.

980
00:37:55,219 --> 00:37:56,996
Ready, set, go!

981
00:37:57,835 --> 00:38:00,888
[Tweedledum and Tweedledee]

982
00:38:01,555 --> 00:38:04,008
Same difference.

983
00:38:04,008 --> 00:38:07,735
[The Passionate Private Gwak returns]

984
00:38:08,498 --> 00:38:12,458
[The Moonlight cast,
channeling their inner child]

985
00:38:12,458 --> 00:38:15,357
[I'm just going to go ahead]

986
00:38:15,357 --> 00:38:17,690
[The obvious fastest swimmer is...]

987
00:38:18,625 --> 00:38:23,465
[this happy seal]

988
00:38:25,545 --> 00:38:28,538
[I wonder if they're following me well?]

989
00:38:29,214 --> 00:38:32,954
[Smooth sailing,
even with You Jung and Soo Bin attached]

990
00:38:34,978 --> 00:38:37,651
We're coming to save you!

991
00:38:37,651 --> 00:38:39,691
[Come, come!]

992
00:38:43,765 --> 00:38:45,211
Why don't we all hold hands?

993
00:38:45,211 --> 00:38:46,949
Let's all hold hands while we swim.

994
00:38:46,949 --> 00:38:48,185
Try lying on your back.

995
00:38:48,185 --> 00:38:49,791
[Hand in hand, floating serenely]
Let's lie down.

996
00:38:49,791 --> 00:38:52,097
Kick your feet, come on.

997
00:38:55,631 --> 00:38:57,231
Who's leading?

998
00:38:57,231 --> 00:38:58,595
Jin Young is.

999
00:38:58,595 --> 00:39:01,874
Why was there a long pause?

1000
00:39:02,598 --> 00:39:05,225
Hey, Bo Gum, do a flip!

1001
00:39:05,225 --> 00:39:07,125
[Will he try again, this time from the boat?]
Yeah, do a flip!

1002
00:39:07,125 --> 00:39:08,882
- I don't think I can.
- No, no.

1003
00:39:08,882 --> 00:39:11,751
Just jump, and flip!

1004
00:39:18,845 --> 00:39:22,418
[After rafting and cooling down
from the summer heat...]

1005
00:39:22,418 --> 00:39:25,638
[land ahoy!]

1006
00:39:25,638 --> 00:39:27,565
Oh, there's a spooky story about this place.

1007
00:39:27,565 --> 00:39:28,891
Have you heard about it? I doubt you have.

1008
00:39:28,891 --> 00:39:30,889
- We haven't.
- Let's tell them. We have to.

1009
00:39:30,889 --> 00:39:32,165
[An urban legend about the Hongcheon river]

1010
00:39:32,165 --> 00:39:33,751
So, if you follow the river downstream...

1011
00:39:33,751 --> 00:39:35,495
- that's the Palbong mountain.
- Yes?

1012
00:39:35,495 --> 00:39:37,465
- See that pointy peak on the far left?
- Yeah.

1013
00:39:37,465 --> 00:39:38,991
- That one, on the left?
- Oh, yeah.

1014
00:39:38,991 --> 00:39:40,765
It's called that because it has eight peaks.

1015
00:39:40,765 --> 00:39:42,718
At the very edge...

1016
00:39:42,718 --> 00:39:44,618
[Gaksi Rock at the edge of Palbong mountain]
there's a boulder called the Gaksi Rock.

1017
00:39:44,618 --> 00:39:46,655
- Gaksi?
- Like, a newlywed bride.

1018
00:39:46,655 --> 00:39:50,983
So this Gaksi Rock is strangely
always shrouded in a veil of darkness.

1019
00:39:53,110 --> 00:39:58,941
There are many pensions around there,
and every night, men go there and drown.

1020
00:39:59,759 --> 00:40:03,310
They say a woman there keeps
luring men in with her singing.

1021
00:40:03,310 --> 00:40:05,592
- Telling them to come in.
- Telling them to come in.

1022
00:40:05,592 --> 00:40:08,719
[The Gaksi Rock ghost who even sings well]
By the time you snap out of it...

1023
00:40:08,719 --> 00:40:09,788
The water is already up to your neck.

1024
00:40:09,788 --> 00:40:12,553
Oppa, why are you so quiet?
Jin Young oppa became so quiet.

1025
00:40:12,553 --> 00:40:14,259
[Cowardly Hyung / 35, weak to water and ghosts]

1026
00:40:14,259 --> 00:40:16,879
- He's scared right now.
- It'll appear after a short walk from here.

1027
00:40:16,879 --> 00:40:18,344
- I'll come back later.
- Okay.

1028
00:40:18,344 --> 00:40:19,999
[Staggering]
Oh, wait a minute.

1029
00:40:19,999 --> 00:40:23,298
[The cowardly hyung's legs give out]
- No, this is weird. - I'm sorry.

1030
00:40:23,298 --> 00:40:25,923
[Ending with the legend of Gaksi Rock...]
Ah, that's so funny.

1031
00:40:25,923 --> 00:40:29,730
[Rafting ends]
- Good job, everyone. - Good job.

1032
00:40:29,730 --> 00:40:35,423
[Time to go grocery shopping after rafting]
Let's go grocery shopping.

1033
00:40:35,423 --> 00:40:37,859
[Bo Gum > Soo Bin]
Is Soo Bin's ear okay?

1034
00:40:37,859 --> 00:40:41,447
[Soo Bin went to the hospital for ear pain]
She's fine, but she's going just in case.

1035
00:40:41,447 --> 00:40:43,879
[Only four people are going shopping]
- She's going? - So just the four of us?

1036
00:40:43,879 --> 00:40:46,499
- Yes. The ingredients...
- Ingredients for baeksuk?

1037
00:40:46,499 --> 00:40:47,963
- Since we're having baeksuk.
- Is it baeksuk?

1038
00:40:47,963 --> 00:40:51,038
[Back in the Moonlight Drawn by Clouds days!]
There was a scene where we ate chicken.

1039
00:40:51,038 --> 00:40:53,212
- Yes. The scene where we eat baeksuk.
- Right?

1040
00:40:53,212 --> 00:40:55,712
- I didn't know he was the Crown Prince.
- Right.

1041
00:40:55,712 --> 00:40:59,423
[The scene at the bench in Jahyundang]
You even cursed at him for not greeting you.

1042
00:40:59,423 --> 00:41:01,119
[The five friends will enjoy it together]
Sorry. It's because so hot now.

1043
00:41:01,119 --> 00:41:03,345
It's hot right now.

1044
00:41:05,071 --> 00:41:07,419
The things that go into baeksuk...

1045
00:41:07,419 --> 00:41:09,139
[The main chef who searched in advance]
- Did you find it? - I found it.

1046
00:41:09,139 --> 00:41:10,939
Oh, yes.

1047
00:41:12,459 --> 00:41:17,545
Water, leeks, garlic, onion,
whole pepper, jujubes, and salt.

1048
00:41:17,545 --> 00:41:19,459
That should be enough.

1049
00:41:19,459 --> 00:41:21,979
And to eat with it...

1050
00:41:21,979 --> 00:41:23,784
Watermelon. Green onion kimchi.

1051
00:41:23,784 --> 00:41:27,899
[Side menus are also ready]
Let's buy chives and make seasoned chives.

1052
00:41:27,899 --> 00:41:30,423
Can you make us shredded potato pancakes?

1053
00:41:30,423 --> 00:41:33,423
[You Jung made them for the members before]
Those potato pancakes were so good.

1054
00:41:33,423 --> 00:41:36,819
[The unforgettable You Jung style pancakes]
Shredded potato pancakes. Shredded.

1055
00:41:36,819 --> 00:41:38,693
- Right. Should I make them?
- Yes.

1056
00:41:38,693 --> 00:41:40,718
I thought you might not want them
since we had potato pancakes earlier.

1057
00:41:40,718 --> 00:41:45,199
Potato pancakes, kimchi pancakes,
or we could make spicy noodles.

1058
00:41:45,199 --> 00:41:48,100
- Spicy noodles.
- Then can you pick just one?

1059
00:41:48,100 --> 00:41:52,941
[Chef You Jung confirms two types of pancakes]
I'll make potato and kimchi pancakes.

1060
00:41:53,923 --> 00:41:56,923
[A refreshing summer day with blue skies]

1061
00:41:56,923 --> 00:42:01,924
[A drive that makes you hum along]

1062
00:42:01,924 --> 00:42:04,039
You seem very excited.

1063
00:42:05,839 --> 00:42:07,499
Is the child free?

1064
00:42:09,299 --> 00:42:10,799
The child.

1065
00:42:11,539 --> 00:42:14,016
Are you saying it is free of charge?

1066
00:42:15,255 --> 00:42:16,545
[Arriving at the market]
We're here.

1067
00:42:16,545 --> 00:42:19,108
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1068
00:42:20,589 --> 00:42:22,979
- Let's go!
- So hot!

1069
00:42:22,979 --> 00:42:26,159
- Hello.
- It's so hot.

1070
00:42:26,159 --> 00:42:28,099
Let's go.

1071
00:42:28,099 --> 00:42:29,859
Can I buy this?

1072
00:42:29,859 --> 00:42:31,579
I really like this.

1073
00:42:31,579 --> 00:42:33,379
- No.
- Why? Just one.

1074
00:42:33,379 --> 00:42:35,773
- Don't buy it.
- Aw, why?

1075
00:42:35,773 --> 00:42:37,944
- Just one.
- Don't buy it.

1076
00:42:38,609 --> 00:42:39,694
You're really not buying it for me?

1077
00:42:39,694 --> 00:42:41,191
- No.
- You're so heartless.

1078
00:42:41,191 --> 00:42:42,991
- We just need two chickens.
- Don't buy things like that.

1079
00:42:42,991 --> 00:42:44,015
Two chickens?

1080
00:42:44,015 --> 00:42:46,423
[Buying ingredients for baeksuk first]
Let's see,

1081
00:42:46,423 --> 00:42:48,923
[+ Chicken 1 + Chicken 2]
- Right? - Yeah.

1082
00:42:48,923 --> 00:42:50,955
[ Chicken, Seasoning,
Veggies, Side dishes, Snacks, Drinks]

1083
00:42:50,955 --> 00:42:53,082
He's letting me buy this.

1084
00:42:53,082 --> 00:42:54,923
What about this?

1085
00:42:54,923 --> 00:42:56,728
[Like a dad who never buys toys]
Put it back.

1086
00:42:56,728 --> 00:43:01,052
We don't need soybean paste,
but we need to buy salt.

1087
00:43:01,052 --> 00:43:02,967
- I'll go get some pepper.
- Whole peppercorns.

1088
00:43:02,967 --> 00:43:05,845
[Shopping goes smoothly under You Jung's lead]
I'll mix green onions, perilla, and chives.

1089
00:43:05,845 --> 00:43:09,769
- Making potato pancakes too might be too hard.
- What? Potato pancakes?

1090
00:43:09,769 --> 00:43:12,215
I think I can make them quickly.

1091
00:43:12,215 --> 00:43:14,384
- Here are the potatoes.
- We need to buy green onions.

1092
00:43:15,396 --> 00:43:18,149
They've pre-portioned the potatoes like this.

1093
00:43:18,149 --> 00:43:19,175
I can slice these up in no time.

1094
00:43:19,175 --> 00:43:21,130
[Potatoes purchased]
I think four will be enough.

1095
00:43:22,423 --> 00:43:25,923
[??? Bo Gum heading somewhere alone]

1096
00:43:28,159 --> 00:43:29,704
Hehe.

1097
00:43:30,411 --> 00:43:33,539
[Caught wandering the snack aisle]
Again, right before a meal.

1098
00:43:33,539 --> 00:43:37,045
Come here. Over here.

1099
00:43:38,007 --> 00:43:39,531
Give it to me.

1100
00:43:39,531 --> 00:43:40,611
Let me have it first.

1101
00:43:40,611 --> 00:43:42,610
- Two?
- No. Just get one.

1102
00:43:42,610 --> 00:43:44,423
Here's the watermelon.

1103
00:43:44,423 --> 00:43:46,211
- Oh, okay!
- We have to eat this.

1104
00:43:46,211 --> 00:43:49,923
- This is delicious too.
- No, no. Come here. No.

1105
00:43:49,923 --> 00:43:52,595
[Worried he won't eat his dinner...]
No, you have to eat dinner.

1106
00:43:52,595 --> 00:43:55,291
Seriously, what's with you guys?

1107
00:43:55,291 --> 00:43:57,423
- It's good.
- You need to eat a proper meal.

1108
00:43:57,423 --> 00:43:59,911
[The snack crackdown squad fails]
I'm telling you, he won't eat dinner now.

1109
00:44:00,831 --> 00:44:02,375
Hello.

1110
00:44:02,375 --> 00:44:04,019
Where are you from?

1111
00:44:04,951 --> 00:44:08,471
[Starting a solo skit while the guys are away]
I think they're filming something here.

1112
00:44:08,471 --> 00:44:12,200
I'm here to pick up a potato mallangi today.

1113
00:44:14,431 --> 00:44:17,233
I'll sneak it onto the counter
so Bo Gum doesn't see.

1114
00:44:17,233 --> 00:44:20,371
[The youngest buys a mallangi
while the guys buy snacks]

1115
00:44:20,371 --> 00:44:21,830
[Enough food for three days]
Did we buy too much?

1116
00:44:21,830 --> 00:44:24,271
The cart looks like a 3-day trip.

1117
00:44:24,271 --> 00:44:26,923
- I know.
- Let's go.

1118
00:44:26,923 --> 00:44:29,423
[Current time 16:30 Shopping finished]

1119
00:44:29,423 --> 00:44:32,423
[Heading back to the lodge with happy hearts]

1120
00:44:32,423 --> 00:44:34,423
[Rustling]

1121
00:44:34,423 --> 00:44:36,271
Isn't that an Akppu?

1122
00:44:36,271 --> 00:44:39,368
[Glancing, Let me see]
This isn't Wapu. It's just a mallangi.

1123
00:44:42,431 --> 00:44:44,411
You didn't let me buy it...

1124
00:44:44,411 --> 00:44:46,403
[Curious now that she bought it]
Let me touch it.

1125
00:44:46,403 --> 00:44:49,037
- I've never seen this before.
- "Teacher," haha.

1126
00:44:50,231 --> 00:44:52,923
[Experiencing new things thanks to her]
So this is what it's like.

1127
00:44:56,660 --> 00:44:58,336
Yujin-i?

1128
00:44:58,336 --> 00:45:00,575
- What?
- Huh?

1129
00:45:00,575 --> 00:45:02,231
It's not even Yujin-li.

1130
00:45:02,231 --> 00:45:03,511
- Right.
- Why Yujin-i?

1131
00:45:03,511 --> 00:45:05,395
Yujin-li? Yujin-i?

1132
00:45:05,395 --> 00:45:07,007
[Suddenly getting scared...]
I'm already scared.

1133
00:45:07,007 --> 00:45:09,385
Why is that scary?

1134
00:45:09,385 --> 00:45:14,023
No, don't you think we saw something wrong
all of us together?

1135
00:45:14,023 --> 00:45:16,591
[Worried they're all possessed]
Something changed.

1136
00:45:16,591 --> 00:45:18,631
We can drop you off there on the way.

1137
00:45:18,631 --> 00:45:20,354
At Gaksi Rock.

1138
00:45:20,354 --> 00:45:24,031
Is Yujin at Gaksi Rock?

1139
00:45:24,031 --> 00:45:26,731
- Is the bride's name Yujin?
- Yes, Ms. Yujin.

1140
00:45:26,731 --> 00:45:28,871
Oppa, I'm Yujin.

1141
00:45:30,211 --> 00:45:33,091
I think those campers are amazing.

1142
00:45:33,091 --> 00:45:34,731
Despite the heat and everything.

1143
00:45:34,731 --> 00:45:36,912
- You said you've tried camping, right?
- Yes.

1144
00:45:36,912 --> 00:45:39,223
Camping used to be my hobby.

1145
00:45:39,223 --> 00:45:41,547
- You went on that pilgrimage is amazing.
- Truly.

1146
00:45:43,045 --> 00:45:46,423
[ An 800 km journey
to Santiago de Compostela, Spain.]

1147
00:45:46,423 --> 00:45:48,211
[With just a backpack]
Roughly how many days did you walk?

1148
00:45:48,211 --> 00:45:52,391
[You Jung walked the pilgrimage for a month]
I walked for exactly 33 days.

1149
00:45:52,391 --> 00:45:58,051
So you just keep walking until find
like a dormitory? Then you eat and sleep?

1150
00:45:58,051 --> 00:45:59,091
Yeah.

1151
00:45:59,091 --> 00:46:04,231
Usually, the people who start on the same day
as I did end up arriving around the same time.

1152
00:46:04,231 --> 00:46:05,471
You meet along the way.

1153
00:46:05,471 --> 00:46:10,111
We meet on the way and often eat together.

1154
00:46:10,111 --> 00:46:13,211
So people often become close friends.

1155
00:46:13,211 --> 00:46:15,471
Even though you mostly walk alone.

1156
00:46:15,471 --> 00:46:20,178
So, being alone in those vast fields
and the wilderness...

1157
00:46:20,178 --> 00:46:22,411
That feeling is really great.

1158
00:46:22,411 --> 00:46:24,731
It makes me feel truly free.

1159
00:46:24,731 --> 00:46:29,231
I can feel that I'm experiencing true freedom.

1160
00:46:33,423 --> 00:46:35,930
[Arrived at the lodge]

1161
00:46:35,930 --> 00:46:38,135
It's so green and lush.

1162
00:46:38,135 --> 00:46:41,018
- Oh my.
- What's this?

1163
00:46:41,018 --> 00:46:43,923
- They prepared a snack for us.
- Corn!

1164
00:46:43,923 --> 00:46:46,671
[Relaxing with corn in the late afternoon]
It's seasoned so well.

1165
00:46:46,671 --> 00:46:47,951
Hyung, if you don't mind...

1166
00:46:47,951 --> 00:46:49,015
Who wants a beer?

1167
00:46:49,015 --> 00:46:50,547
[Of course]
Can I lie down on your lap for a bit?

1168
00:46:50,547 --> 00:46:53,231
Who wants a beer?
Do you want some corn beer?

1169
00:46:53,231 --> 00:46:55,491
- Is it cold?
- Do you want to share this?

1170
00:46:56,951 --> 00:46:59,191
Corn with corn beer is a great combo.

1171
00:46:59,191 --> 00:47:02,131
But were you really scared earlier?

1172
00:47:02,131 --> 00:47:03,655
Of course.

1173
00:47:03,655 --> 00:47:06,402
- When? While rafting?
- I was terrified.

1174
00:47:06,402 --> 00:47:08,337
But you seemed to enjoy it later.

1175
00:47:08,337 --> 00:47:09,505
I got used to it.

1176
00:47:09,505 --> 00:47:15,427
I eventually realized how safe life vests are.

1177
00:47:15,427 --> 00:47:21,103
There was no one else around,
so swimming in the river was nice.

1178
00:47:22,811 --> 00:47:26,691
I think it was my first time
swimming in a valley like that.

1179
00:47:26,691 --> 00:47:28,232
It was quite peaceful.

1180
00:47:28,232 --> 00:47:30,943
[Even Jin Young, who's afraid of water]
It really was.

1181
00:47:30,943 --> 00:47:32,486
Let's all put on our sunglasses.

1182
00:47:32,486 --> 00:47:36,887
[A beautiful and peaceful time together]
Sun Jae, try lying down there.

1183
00:47:36,887 --> 00:47:39,660
- It was fun.
- Yeah.

1184
00:47:39,660 --> 00:47:42,079
Jumping off was a bit scary, though...

1185
00:47:42,079 --> 00:47:44,047
I remember Bo Gum jumping.

1186
00:47:44,047 --> 00:47:49,003
- Climbing up there.
- I just couldn't do it right.

1187
00:47:49,003 --> 00:47:51,823
[Wanna Be]

1188
00:47:51,823 --> 00:47:55,759
[Reality]

1189
00:47:55,759 --> 00:47:58,631
[Chairman Park's unexpected clumsy moment]
He fell kind of like this.

1190
00:47:58,631 --> 00:48:02,051
- Didn't you jump on trampolines as a kid?
- Trampolines?

1191
00:48:02,811 --> 00:48:05,591
- You've never been on one?
- Not even once.

1192
00:48:05,591 --> 00:48:07,871
But on a trampoline, you can do this.

1193
00:48:07,871 --> 00:48:10,315
- People do it all the time.
- Like rolling around?

1194
00:48:10,315 --> 00:48:13,523
- You can do three or four flips.
- Really?

1195
00:48:13,523 --> 00:48:17,591
[Rolling down]
Come down now. Yes.

1196
00:48:17,591 --> 00:48:19,811
[Bouncing with pride]
- That's amazing. Like a gymnast.

1197
00:48:19,811 --> 00:48:21,571
- It's addictive.
- This is so delicious.

1198
00:48:21,571 --> 00:48:23,171
- That's your third one.
- Huh?

1199
00:48:23,171 --> 00:48:26,511
- How much do you weigh?
- Me? About 66 kg?

1200
00:48:26,511 --> 00:48:27,891
- Sixty-six?
- Yeah.

1201
00:48:27,891 --> 00:48:29,391
- That's crazy.
- You're so thin.

1202
00:48:29,391 --> 00:48:32,087
You're in such good shape.
I thought you'd be in the 70s.

1203
00:48:32,087 --> 00:48:35,391
- Really?
- I was 65 kg during Moonlight.

1204
00:48:35,391 --> 00:48:37,111
What? You were 65 kg back then?

1205
00:48:37,111 --> 00:48:40,523
But now I'm 73... 74... 75 kg.

1206
00:48:40,523 --> 00:48:43,348
[The number keeps going up...]
You're thin too.

1207
00:48:43,348 --> 00:48:44,455
I'm 76 kg.

1208
00:48:44,455 --> 00:48:47,478
[Actually, he's 76 kg]
To be honest, I'm 76 kg.

1209
00:48:47,478 --> 00:48:51,399
[Relatable: understating his weight]
Wow, and you said 66.

1210
00:48:51,399 --> 00:48:54,199
- Were you 17 back then?
- Yes.

1211
00:48:54,199 --> 00:48:56,779
Did it feel different when you turned 20?

1212
00:48:56,779 --> 00:49:01,543
We went to the KBS Drama Awards
to present an award.

1213
00:49:01,543 --> 00:49:04,870
Remember the Top Excellence Award?
I wore a light purple dress.

1214
00:49:04,870 --> 00:49:07,223
That was the day I turned 20.

1215
00:49:07,223 --> 00:49:08,823
[December 31st!]
It was the 31st.

1216
00:49:08,823 --> 00:49:11,899
[You Jung turned 20 in the waiting room]
Midnight passed while I was there.

1217
00:49:11,899 --> 00:49:15,939
I'll work hard like my seniors
to stand here one day.

1218
00:49:15,939 --> 00:49:18,579
Park Bo Gum, please announce the winner.

1219
00:49:18,579 --> 00:49:23,839
After that, I went to Itaewon with my mom
and sister and had a drink.

1220
00:49:23,839 --> 00:49:26,519
I cried because I didn't want to turn 20.

1221
00:49:26,519 --> 00:49:28,099
- Really?
- Why?

1222
00:49:28,099 --> 00:49:31,313
I was dying to become
an adult as soon as possible.

1223
00:49:31,313 --> 00:49:35,479
I was a bit scared of becoming an adult.

1224
00:49:36,423 --> 00:49:39,423
[After their long chat...]

1225
00:49:39,423 --> 00:49:42,074
[Soo Bin returns from the hospital]

1226
00:49:42,074 --> 00:49:43,863
Are you okay?

1227
00:49:43,863 --> 00:49:45,679
I don't think it's a big deal.

1228
00:49:45,679 --> 00:49:47,871
Was your ear weak to begin with?

1229
00:49:47,871 --> 00:49:50,958
Maybe it's because
I kept calling her a herbivore?

1230
00:49:50,958 --> 00:49:54,693
[The Five Are Reunited Upon Soo Bin's Return]

1231
00:49:54,693 --> 00:49:57,924
- Shall we start getting ready for dinner?
- Sure.

1232
00:49:57,924 --> 00:50:02,165
[Today's Menu: Baeksuk, Kimchi Jeon...]
Prepare the green onions and Baeksuk.

1233
00:50:02,165 --> 00:50:05,883
- There's not much to prep for Baeksuk, right?
- No, you just put everything in whole.

1234
00:50:05,883 --> 00:50:09,476
I think we just need to wash the chicken.

1235
00:50:09,476 --> 00:50:11,599
[Taking out the chicken first]

1236
00:50:11,599 --> 00:50:15,476
[Dong Yeon naturally takes charge of Baeksuk]
The chicken...

1237
00:50:16,644 --> 00:50:19,236
[Bo Gum & Soo Bin prep the rest]
- Should I open this? - Sure.

1238
00:50:19,236 --> 00:50:21,314
Can I peel the onion?

1239
00:50:21,314 --> 00:50:22,906
No, put it in whole.

1240
00:50:22,906 --> 00:50:25,267
- Can I peel it?
- Put them all in whole.

1241
00:50:26,076 --> 00:50:28,879
- Can I take off this packaging?
- No.

1242
00:50:28,879 --> 00:50:30,327
Can I take off this packaging?

1243
00:50:30,327 --> 00:50:32,959
No, put it in whole.

1244
00:50:32,959 --> 00:50:36,230
That's where the flavor comes from.

1245
00:50:36,230 --> 00:50:39,063
[They almost ate Baeksuk with plastic in it]
Put this in whole.

1246
00:50:39,063 --> 00:50:42,103
[Prep complete as per Chef You Jung's orders]

1247
00:50:42,103 --> 00:50:47,141
[Time to stuff the prepped chicken]
I should put the ginkgo nuts in first.

1248
00:50:47,141 --> 00:50:51,185
[Ginkgo nuts, chestnuts, jujubes]

1249
00:50:51,185 --> 00:50:55,195
[Baeksuk prep is done]
Now we just need to prep the vegetables.

1250
00:50:55,195 --> 00:50:57,180
- I'll go light the fire, everyone.
- Okay.

1251
00:50:57,180 --> 00:51:00,972
[The Baeksuk will cook in a cauldron outside]

1252
00:51:00,972 --> 00:51:03,169
Are you okay with lighting the fire?

1253
00:51:03,169 --> 00:51:05,991
- Why?
- Aren't you scared?

1254
00:51:05,991 --> 00:51:08,243
[Oh, please]
Since you're scared of water, fire is also...

1255
00:51:08,243 --> 00:51:12,028
- I'm strong against fire.
- It's the opposite.

1256
00:51:12,737 --> 00:51:14,960
[Jin Young & Soo Bin stack the firewood]

1257
00:51:14,960 --> 00:51:16,455
- Just throw it in.
- Just throw it in?

1258
00:51:16,455 --> 00:51:18,143
I think you can just throw it in.

1259
00:51:18,143 --> 00:51:21,039
Can I just throw it in?
Don't we need to stack it, Oppa?

1260
00:51:21,039 --> 00:51:22,899
- It probably won't matter.
- Really?

1261
00:51:22,899 --> 00:51:24,979
You seem a bit skeptical?

1262
00:51:24,979 --> 00:51:27,799
[She is indeed skeptical]
- Right? - Have you done this before?

1263
00:51:27,799 --> 00:51:30,675
- And...
- They look like they know how to cook.

1264
00:51:30,675 --> 00:51:32,017
Not at all, Oppa.

1265
00:51:32,017 --> 00:51:35,065
No? Not at all?

1266
00:51:37,898 --> 00:51:39,759
Will those two be okay?

1267
00:51:39,759 --> 00:51:43,161
I'm suddenly worried
about leaving them by the fire.

1268
00:51:45,339 --> 00:51:47,841
[Fire Jin Young takes out the torch]

1269
00:51:47,841 --> 00:51:50,332
[He lights it up with confidence]

1270
00:51:52,287 --> 00:51:54,948
- But it's actually already done.
- Eh, really?

1271
00:51:54,948 --> 00:51:56,683
[Success in just 3 seconds...?]
It's lit.

1272
00:51:56,683 --> 00:51:59,253
The fire caught on so well at once.

1273
00:51:59,253 --> 00:52:01,734
- Wow, it lit so well.
- That was simple.

1274
00:52:01,734 --> 00:52:04,258
[Immediately putting the ingredients in]

1275
00:52:04,258 --> 00:52:07,259
[Simmer for an hour and it's done]
Then we just boil it like this for an hour.

1276
00:52:07,259 --> 00:52:08,262
I'm all done, man.

1277
00:52:08,262 --> 00:52:09,930
[Fire Jin Young returns confidently]
That's amazing.

1278
00:52:09,930 --> 00:52:13,394
- As long as it's not water.
- As long as it's not water.

1279
00:52:13,394 --> 00:52:14,810
[Meanwhile, Main Chef You Jung]

1280
00:52:14,810 --> 00:52:19,111
[Slice up the chives and perilla leaves,
quickly making the seasoning]

1281
00:52:19,111 --> 00:52:21,602
- What's this?
- Scallion salad.

1282
00:52:21,602 --> 00:52:25,040
[Scallion salad with perilla leaves & chives]
I just added perilla leaves and chives.

1283
00:52:25,040 --> 00:52:27,489
Now we just need to put the kimchi on a plate.

1284
00:52:27,489 --> 00:52:28,573
It's in the fridge.

1285
00:52:28,573 --> 00:52:31,208
You used everything for the kimchi pancake?

1286
00:52:31,208 --> 00:52:33,208
Yes. I've prepared it all.

1287
00:52:33,996 --> 00:52:36,451
[One hour ago, during break time]

1288
00:52:36,451 --> 00:52:39,045
[Quietly peeling potatoes alone]

1289
00:52:39,045 --> 00:52:41,211
[Shredding the potatoes]

1290
00:52:41,211 --> 00:52:43,725
[You Jung prepared the pancake batter]

1291
00:52:43,725 --> 00:52:46,461
[Bo Gum joins her soon after]

1292
00:52:46,461 --> 00:52:48,343
[Kimchi pancake batter]

1293
00:52:48,343 --> 00:52:53,373
[They gave up their rest for their friends]
Should I take out the watermelon?

1294
00:52:53,373 --> 00:52:56,251
[Dinner prep is on track thanks to them]
I've prepared everything.

1295
00:52:56,251 --> 00:52:59,340
Is there anything else I should do?

1296
00:52:59,340 --> 00:53:02,243
[Only the pancakes are left]
No. I just need to fry the pancakes.

1297
00:53:02,243 --> 00:53:04,679
[Glancing]

1298
00:53:05,780 --> 00:53:08,783
[He rushes to get up and go outside...?]

1299
00:53:10,239 --> 00:53:13,243
[The cauldron is smoking like crazy]
Wait, is there a fire?

1300
00:53:13,243 --> 00:53:17,943
[Checking the chicken soup]
It's not boiling at all.

1301
00:53:17,943 --> 00:53:20,375
[Only smoke, the soup isn't cooking]
It's not boiling at all.

1302
00:53:20,375 --> 00:53:23,699
[Damp firewood prevents a proper fire]
The fire isn't strong. Maybe it's damp.

1303
00:53:23,699 --> 00:53:28,091
[Appearing with kindling]
Because it's humid.

1304
00:53:28,091 --> 00:53:29,837
[Focusing]

1305
00:53:29,837 --> 00:53:34,182
[Struggling to save the chicken soup]

1306
00:53:36,811 --> 00:53:39,436
[Passionate photographer captures the crisis]

1307
00:53:39,436 --> 00:53:42,413
[The struggle for the soup is documented]

1308
00:53:42,413 --> 00:53:44,783
Wow, it's much stronger than before.

1309
00:53:44,783 --> 00:53:48,323
No joke. It's finally burning well.

1310
00:53:48,323 --> 00:53:50,325
[Checking the soup]
It's boiling.

1311
00:53:50,325 --> 00:53:53,533
[The chicken soup finally starts to boil]

1312
00:53:53,533 --> 00:53:57,496
[You Jung is about to fry the pancakes]
But what should I do about this?

1313
00:53:57,496 --> 00:54:00,072
I want to turn on the one next to it too.

1314
00:54:00,775 --> 00:54:03,805
[Sweet Chairman Park helps immediately]

1315
00:54:03,805 --> 00:54:06,474
[Starting to fry the pancakes]

1316
00:54:06,474 --> 00:54:09,711
[Spreading the batter on the pan]

1317
00:54:09,711 --> 00:54:12,594
[Adding one more pan?]

1318
00:54:12,594 --> 00:54:16,431
[Cover it with a lid to keep it moist inside]

1319
00:54:16,431 --> 00:54:19,004
[10 Minutes Later]

1320
00:54:19,004 --> 00:54:20,023
Oh, it looks delicious.

1321
00:54:20,023 --> 00:54:22,437
[The potato pancake is crispy outside,
soft inside, and done]

1322
00:54:22,437 --> 00:54:24,109
[Sizzle]

1323
00:54:25,293 --> 00:54:27,996
[Kimchi pancakes are ready in a flash]

1324
00:54:27,996 --> 00:54:29,778
[A short break while the baeksuk boils]

1325
00:54:29,778 --> 00:54:32,114
[Soo Bin wants to play...]
Should I... play the accompaniment?

1326
00:54:32,114 --> 00:54:34,002
- Should I?
- Oh, you know how to play it?

1327
00:54:34,002 --> 00:54:36,681
[Sweet Chairman Park sits right at the piano]
Ready, set, go.

1328
00:54:38,373 --> 00:54:40,038
Oh.

1329
00:54:40,038 --> 00:54:41,770
Oh!

1330
00:54:44,448 --> 00:54:47,521
[Staring]

1331
00:54:47,521 --> 00:54:49,781
Why is the song so sweet?

1332
00:54:50,685 --> 00:54:54,898
[Soo Bin and Bo Gum's sweet ensemble]
The song is so sweet.

1333
00:54:58,793 --> 00:55:00,899
[The summer night ensemble ends]

1334
00:55:02,602 --> 00:55:06,473
Since it's summer, we should add red ginseng
to boost our health.

1335
00:55:06,473 --> 00:55:07,858
[A must-have for summer baeksuk]
Awesome!

1336
00:55:07,858 --> 00:55:09,192
I just need to add this?

1337
00:55:09,192 --> 00:55:10,360
Yes.

1338
00:55:10,360 --> 00:55:11,923
It's a real health food.

1339
00:55:11,923 --> 00:55:13,229
Exactly.

1340
00:55:17,015 --> 00:55:19,161
- It'll be so good for our health.
- I'm curious.

1341
00:55:19,161 --> 00:55:22,289
- About the taste.
- Let's get healthy.

1342
00:55:22,289 --> 00:55:24,905
Should we take the baeksuk out now?

1343
00:55:24,905 --> 00:55:29,536
[Will the baeksuk be a success?]
- Someone help me. - Okay.

1344
00:55:29,536 --> 00:55:31,276
It looks delicious.

1345
00:55:33,923 --> 00:55:36,862
[The baeksuk is cooked to perfection]

1346
00:55:36,862 --> 00:55:39,556
Wow, hey, it looks delicious.

1347
00:55:39,556 --> 00:55:41,469
Wow, it turned out better than I thought.

1348
00:55:41,469 --> 00:55:44,227
It's no joke. The broth is amazing.

1349
00:55:44,227 --> 00:55:46,560
[Taking out the impressive baeksuk]
Is the broth good?

1350
00:55:46,560 --> 00:55:49,234
Wow, this is the main dish.

1351
00:55:49,234 --> 00:55:52,923
[Placed in the center of the table]
It turned out so well. Amazing, right?

1352
00:55:52,923 --> 00:55:55,923
[10 years ago - The baeksuk Ra On made]
Here.

1353
00:55:55,923 --> 00:56:00,329
[The main menu for the 10th anniversary dinner]
Wow, it looks so good.

1354
00:56:00,329 --> 00:56:02,923
[The rest of the table is full too]
It's a real feast.

1355
00:56:02,923 --> 00:56:06,232
[You Jung's crispy pancakes and...]
You're so generous. How many did you fry?

1356
00:56:06,232 --> 00:56:09,453
[Scallions, the perfect match for baeksuk]
Invite the whole neighborhood.

1357
00:56:09,453 --> 00:56:12,313
[Bo Gum's spicy noodles & Jin Young's lamb]
Wow, it's so hearty.

1358
00:56:12,313 --> 00:56:14,257
[A feast prepared with great care]
Come on, let's eat.

1359
00:56:14,257 --> 00:56:16,964
- Sounds good.
- Let's sit.

1360
00:56:16,964 --> 00:56:19,129
- You worked so hard making this.
- Good job, everyone.

1361
00:56:19,129 --> 00:56:20,720
Well done.

1362
00:56:20,720 --> 00:56:23,783
- Let's eat.
- Thank you for the meal.

1363
00:56:23,783 --> 00:56:26,186
- Enjoy your meal.
- Thank you for the meal.

1364
00:56:26,186 --> 00:56:28,813
Let's take a photo first.

1365
00:56:28,813 --> 00:56:33,109
[The five of them enjoy a baeksuk feast]
- Yes. - Okay.

1366
00:56:33,109 --> 00:56:35,129
Hurry and enjoy your meal.

1367
00:56:35,129 --> 00:56:36,653
I'll carve the baeksuk.

1368
00:56:36,653 --> 00:56:38,923
[Dong Yeon carves the chicken for everyone]
Yes, thank you.

1369
00:56:38,923 --> 00:56:41,618
[Picking out the biggest chicken leg]
No, it's okay.

1370
00:56:41,618 --> 00:56:43,499
- Chef.
- Thank you.

1371
00:56:43,499 --> 00:56:46,469
You have a leg, and our patient
should have one too.

1372
00:56:46,469 --> 00:56:48,208
[Sharing the baeksuk one by one]
But I'm fine without a leg.

1373
00:56:48,208 --> 00:56:53,261
[You Jung takes a bite first]
No, it's okay, really.

1374
00:56:54,009 --> 00:56:56,716
Wow, this baeksuk is so delicious.

1375
00:56:56,716 --> 00:56:58,313
It is, right?

1376
00:56:58,313 --> 00:57:00,929
[Bo Gum takes a bite off the bone]
It's good.

1377
00:57:00,929 --> 00:57:03,007
[Cleanly deboned]

1378
00:57:03,007 --> 00:57:04,833
So good.

1379
00:57:04,833 --> 00:57:08,909
- This is real health food.
- It's got everything.

1380
00:57:09,563 --> 00:57:11,808
[Dong Yeon tries it too.]
How's the broth?

1381
00:57:12,896 --> 00:57:13,964
Is it good?

1382
00:57:13,964 --> 00:57:15,669
I can stay up all night!

1383
00:57:15,669 --> 00:57:17,487
Really? That much?

1384
00:57:17,487 --> 00:57:20,049
[Deep exclamations unlike a 20-something]
Do you feel energized?

1385
00:57:20,049 --> 00:57:22,423
You sound like a real dad.

1386
00:57:22,423 --> 00:57:26,413
[Dad...?]
He was an uncle just this morning.

1387
00:57:26,413 --> 00:57:28,206
Wow, man, this is...

1388
00:57:28,206 --> 00:57:31,249
Seriously, try it. It makes you like this.

1389
00:57:31,249 --> 00:57:33,509
- But eating this baeksuk...
- Yeah.

1390
00:57:33,509 --> 00:57:36,269
Do you remember that line at Jahyeondang?

1391
00:57:36,269 --> 00:57:37,853
The one where we talk behind his back?

1392
00:57:37,853 --> 00:57:38,769
The Crown Prince.

1393
00:57:38,769 --> 00:57:41,361
[Lines that come to mind while eating]
The Crown Prince's nickname.

1394
00:57:41,361 --> 00:57:44,041
- What was it?
- Ddong-gung-jeon?

1395
00:57:46,933 --> 00:57:51,452
Do you know the Crown Prince's nickname?

1396
00:57:51,452 --> 00:57:52,912
[Lee Yeong | Flower Prince?]
Flower Prince?

1397
00:57:52,912 --> 00:57:54,806
[Byeong Yeon | Ddong-gung-jeon]
Ddong-gung-jeon.

1398
00:57:55,442 --> 00:57:58,903
I knew everyone knew about it.

1399
00:57:58,903 --> 00:58:00,280
Then what about the other one?

1400
00:58:00,280 --> 00:58:02,365
Half-human, half-beast.

1401
00:58:02,365 --> 00:58:03,950
That's right.

1402
00:58:03,950 --> 00:58:06,244
- Right, right.
- That was the funniest part for me.

1403
00:58:06,244 --> 00:58:10,948
Since Dong Yeon is laughing...
"Oh, you know how to laugh?"

1404
00:58:10,948 --> 00:58:13,960
"I thought there was something
wrong with your face."

1405
00:58:13,960 --> 00:58:15,295
Right, right.

1406
00:58:15,295 --> 00:58:19,924
[Byeong Yeon laughs for the first time]
"Is he really that vicious and greedy?"

1407
00:58:19,924 --> 00:58:21,972
Hey, seriously!

1408
00:58:23,470 --> 00:58:25,969
"You laughed? Well, I'll be."

1409
00:58:25,969 --> 00:58:29,923
"I thought there was something
wrong with your face."

1410
00:58:29,923 --> 00:58:32,169
"What does the back of the
Crown Prince's head look like?"

1411
00:58:32,169 --> 00:58:33,829
"It's quite a sight."

1412
00:58:33,829 --> 00:58:36,232
"I thought there was something
wrong with your face."

1413
00:58:36,232 --> 00:58:40,629
- Right, right.
- The lines are so good.

1414
00:58:40,629 --> 00:58:43,769
But back then, I felt so much
responsibility and pressure.

1415
00:58:43,769 --> 00:58:45,117
While filming the drama?

1416
00:58:45,117 --> 00:58:46,429
That's how I felt.

1417
00:58:46,429 --> 00:58:52,248
But back then, You Jung was so
accommodating and took good care of me.

1418
00:58:52,248 --> 00:58:56,961
I thought, "Even if it's hard, it won't be
as hard as it is for You Jung."

1419
00:58:56,961 --> 00:59:01,423
Because your character had to go through
so many emotional shifts.

1420
00:59:01,423 --> 00:59:05,470
But even then, she'd always give me
xylitol whenever she came to the set.

1421
00:59:05,470 --> 00:59:07,639
- She took such good care of people.
- I did?

1422
00:59:07,639 --> 00:59:10,395
Yes, you. Even though you were
probably having a harder time.

1423
00:59:10,395 --> 00:59:13,463
Right. That's why I felt like
she was more like an adult.

1424
00:59:13,463 --> 00:59:14,829
Like Dr. Oh Eun Young.

1425
00:59:14,829 --> 00:59:17,857
I think that's how she got
the nickname Dr. Oh Eun Young.

1426
00:59:17,857 --> 00:59:21,319
In my heart, Dong Yeon was always
such a playful character.

1427
00:59:21,319 --> 00:59:24,923
When I look back at how we were then,

1428
00:59:24,923 --> 00:59:27,923
Dong Yeon was always smiling.

1429
00:59:27,923 --> 00:59:30,671
[Dong Yeon never lost his smile]
So that really touched me.

1430
00:59:32,580 --> 00:59:34,416
I was really thankful back then.

1431
00:59:34,416 --> 00:59:38,378
I didn't have much time to prepare
before we suddenly started filming.

1432
00:59:38,378 --> 00:59:40,614
And since I had the most scenes with you,

1433
00:59:40,614 --> 00:59:44,926
I was so grateful that you made me
feel so comfortable.

1434
00:59:44,926 --> 00:59:49,097
But what I'm really thankful for is that
we practically lived on that set.

1435
00:59:49,097 --> 00:59:53,729
- We'd eat and wash at the bathhouse.
- Right, we'd wash at the sauna.

1436
00:59:53,729 --> 00:59:57,397
The dressing room was
on the second floor of the set.

1437
00:59:57,397 --> 01:00:00,161
[The dressing room where they napped]
We'd sleep there with the AC on...

1438
01:00:00,161 --> 01:00:03,825
And one time, Dong Yeon left me a letter.

1439
01:00:03,825 --> 01:00:06,589
I did? What did I write?

1440
01:00:06,589 --> 01:00:07,769
Should I show you the letter?

1441
01:00:07,769 --> 01:00:09,613
Why would you show that?

1442
01:00:09,613 --> 01:00:12,723
- You still have it?
- I still have it.

1443
01:00:12,723 --> 01:00:14,989
[Dong Yeon's letter, kept for 10 years]
"Hyung, I'm heading to Suwon now."

1444
01:00:14,989 --> 01:00:18,789
"You were sleeping so soundly like a baby
angel that I couldn't bear to wake you."

1445
01:00:18,789 --> 01:00:21,329
"We're parting for now, but we'll
definitely meet again."

1446
01:00:21,329 --> 01:00:22,672
"I love you. Thank you."

1447
01:00:22,672 --> 01:00:25,049
Parting for just a few days?

1448
01:00:25,049 --> 01:00:28,269
[Sad to part even for a moment]
It was probably only for a few hours.

1449
01:00:28,269 --> 01:00:32,640
[A sweltering summer night]
Wow, it really is hot. I need another shower.

1450
01:00:32,640 --> 01:00:34,768
That'll be my fourth shower today.

1451
01:00:34,768 --> 01:00:36,519
How did you shower four times?

1452
01:00:36,519 --> 01:00:38,289
- Once in the morning.
- After waking up.

1453
01:00:38,289 --> 01:00:40,509
- And then? After the water activities.
- After the water activities.

1454
01:00:40,509 --> 01:00:42,269
- And then you did it again?
- That's only the third time.

1455
01:00:42,269 --> 01:00:43,529
Is that so important?

1456
01:00:43,529 --> 01:00:46,249
I'm just saying I showered a lot.

1457
01:00:46,249 --> 01:00:47,773
Sorry, sorry.

1458
01:00:47,773 --> 01:00:49,809
[Snapping because of the heat]
I'm just hot right now.

1459
01:00:49,809 --> 01:00:52,674
Hahaha, sorry, sorry.

1460
01:00:52,674 --> 01:00:54,923
It's like watching a dating reality show.

1461
01:00:54,923 --> 01:00:57,415
[EXchange: Gurmi Edition]
EXchange.

1462
01:00:57,415 --> 01:01:01,989
If you hadn't asked how many times I
showered, we wouldn't be acting like this.

1463
01:01:01,989 --> 01:01:05,609
If you'd told me it was that important,
I would've apologized already.

1464
01:01:05,609 --> 01:01:08,709
Why are you bringing this up here?
Just say you're sorry.

1465
01:01:10,669 --> 01:01:12,423
Thank you for the meal.

1466
01:01:12,423 --> 01:01:14,957
[After a delightful meal]
Thank you for the meal.

1467
01:01:16,223 --> 01:01:20,573
[The air cools as night falls]
It's much better now.

1468
01:01:20,573 --> 01:01:23,293
- Yeah, compared to before.
- This is amazing.

1469
01:01:23,882 --> 01:01:25,673
Wait, what?

1470
01:01:25,673 --> 01:01:28,349
- Look at that!
- Why?

1471
01:01:28,349 --> 01:01:30,933
- Those are sky lanterns.
- Sky lanterns!

1472
01:01:30,933 --> 01:01:32,723
Where?

1473
01:01:32,723 --> 01:01:37,873
[Colorful lanterns awaiting the Gurmis]
They're so pretty.

1474
01:01:38,513 --> 01:01:40,667
Wow, I'm touched.

1475
01:01:40,667 --> 01:01:42,506
[One of the many famous scenes]
Dear Heavens,

1476
01:01:42,506 --> 01:01:46,723
[from ]
Please grant our village a bountiful harvest!

1477
01:01:46,723 --> 01:01:50,423
[The specially remembered night
of the Lantern Festival]

1478
01:01:50,423 --> 01:01:53,822
[The moment Lee Yeong and Ra On grew closer]

1479
01:01:54,423 --> 01:01:57,066
[The Gurmis gathered for the Lantern Festival]
The memories just keep coming back, seriously.

1480
01:01:58,249 --> 01:01:59,657
What's this?

1481
01:01:59,657 --> 01:02:01,157
What's going on?

1482
01:02:03,123 --> 01:02:05,146
[Bo Gum is suddenly handed a microphone...?]
Why?

1483
01:02:05,146 --> 01:02:06,753
- What is it?
- What's happening?

1484
01:02:06,753 --> 01:02:07,902
- What's this?
- Nice to meet you.

1485
01:02:07,902 --> 01:02:09,988
[What is this situation?]
Oh, what's this?

1486
01:02:09,988 --> 01:02:11,723
Should I stand up?

1487
01:02:11,723 --> 01:02:14,158
[Everyone is confused by the situation]
Should I stand up?

1488
01:02:14,158 --> 01:02:15,854
- Should I sit down?
- No, what is this?

1489
01:02:15,854 --> 01:02:16,909
- What is it?
- Yes.

1490
01:02:16,909 --> 01:02:19,330
- Live broadcast. Music...
- Music Bank?

1491
01:02:19,330 --> 01:02:20,600
No, no.

1492
01:02:20,600 --> 01:02:23,613
It's Gurmi Cantabile.

1493
01:02:25,423 --> 01:02:30,592
[A special event prepared by former MC Bo Gum]
I'm your surprise MC for today, Park Bo Gum.

1494
01:02:30,592 --> 01:02:33,753
[Full of anticipation]
Awesome!

1495
01:02:33,753 --> 01:02:37,551
The reason I'm holding
the microphone on this meaningful day

1496
01:02:37,551 --> 01:02:39,217
is because!

1497
01:02:39,217 --> 01:02:41,902
To celebrate the 10th anniversary of Gurmi...

1498
01:02:41,902 --> 01:02:42,854
I knew it.

1499
01:02:42,854 --> 01:02:44,423
- Exactly.
- I knew it.

1500
01:02:44,423 --> 01:02:47,872
[A special guest who came all this way?]
We have a very special guest here today.

1501
01:02:47,872 --> 01:02:53,051
When I heard who the guest was,
I thought, "Wow, they're coming?"

1502
01:02:53,051 --> 01:02:55,447
[Is it that surprising?]
Wow, they're coming?

1503
01:02:55,447 --> 01:02:56,653
Really?

1504
01:02:56,653 --> 01:02:58,077
- Is it Cheon Ho Jin?
- Really?

1505
01:02:58,077 --> 01:02:59,013
Cheon Ho Jin.

1506
01:02:59,013 --> 01:03:01,073
I was so nervous and excited.

1507
01:03:01,073 --> 01:03:02,113
Cheon Ho Jin!

1508
01:03:02,113 --> 01:03:04,513
I miss you, Cheon Ho Jin.

1509
01:03:04,513 --> 01:03:09,723
Now, the guest who will make Gurmi Cantabile
shine even brighter.

1510
01:03:10,465 --> 01:03:15,293
Please welcome them
with a big round of applause.

1511
01:03:15,293 --> 01:03:19,373
♫ I swallow my heart ♫

1512
01:03:19,373 --> 01:03:22,857
♫ Holding a white moonflower ♫

1513
01:03:22,857 --> 01:03:25,093
What? They're going to sing?

1514
01:03:25,093 --> 01:03:26,923
- Isn't that Gummy?
- Really?

1515
01:03:26,923 --> 01:03:29,649
[Who is this surprise guest?]
I think it's a duet.

1516
01:03:29,649 --> 01:03:30,693
I will not allow it.

1517
01:03:30,693 --> 01:03:32,350
[Reliving a classic scene]
She is my person.

1518
01:03:32,350 --> 01:03:33,493
Let's go.

1519
01:03:33,493 --> 01:03:34,993
I will not allow it.

1520
01:03:36,115 --> 01:03:37,611
She is my person.

1521
01:03:39,423 --> 01:03:42,253
[Behind-the-scenes stories after 10 years]
Did your head hit it?

1522
01:03:42,253 --> 01:03:44,082
I really liked this scene.

1523
01:03:44,082 --> 01:03:45,773
Do you still watch it by any chance?

1524
01:03:45,773 --> 01:03:48,087
- I think I watched it recently.
- Really?

1525
01:03:48,087 --> 01:03:49,953
[Honesty that never disappoints]
Exactly.

1526
01:03:49,953 --> 01:03:53,673
I felt so bad for Bo Gum in that scene.

1527
01:03:53,673 --> 01:03:57,843
Back then, the set felt like
it would last forever.

1528
01:03:57,843 --> 01:04:00,233
Since we'll have more time
together in the future...

1529
01:04:00,233 --> 01:04:01,443
Thank you.

1530
01:04:01,443 --> 01:04:03,768
Thank you.

1531
01:04:03,768 --> 01:04:08,123
[The Moonlight crew let loose at night]
Rock, paper, scissors!

1532
01:04:08,123 --> 01:04:09,723
[Chairman Park gets his groove on]

1533
01:04:10,650 --> 01:04:13,406
[The Moonlight crew's endless night]

1534
01:04:16,219 --> 01:04:19,072
It's like wearing an old school uniform
after graduating.

1535
01:04:19,072 --> 01:04:20,886
[The crew returns to their 10-year-old looks]
We meet again after ten years.

1536
01:04:20,886 --> 01:04:23,466
The belt feels smaller than back then.

1537
01:04:23,466 --> 01:04:24,831
I think the clothes got bigger.

1538
01:04:24,831 --> 01:04:26,896
- I felt like we've matured.
- We have matured.

1539
01:04:26,896 --> 01:04:29,036
[The crew's special time travel begins]
It feels really strange.

1540
01:04:29,036 --> 01:04:31,156
What will the next ten years be like?
